  "questions": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Regulation of speech",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A city ordinance makes the city building inspector responsible for ensuring that all buildings in that city are kept up to building code standards and requires the inspector to refer for prosecution all known building code violations. Another ordinance provides that the city building inspector may be discharged for \"good cause.\" The building inspector took a newspaper reporter through a number of run-down buildings in a slum neighborhood. After using various epithets and slurs to describe the occupants of these buildings, the building inspector stated to the reporter: \"I do not even try to get these buildings up to code or to have their owners prosecuted for code violations because if these buildings are repaired, the people who live in them will just wreck them again.\" The reporter published these statements in a story in the local newspaper. The building inspector admitted he made the statements.\nOn the basis of these statements, the city council discharged the building inspector.\nIs the action of the city council constitutional?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because the statements were lawful comments on a matter of public concern.",
        "B": "No, because the statements were published in a newspaper that is protected by the First and Fourteenth Amendments.",
        "C": "Yes, because the building inspector is a government employee and a person holding such a position may not make public comments inconsistent with current governmental policy.",
        "D": "Yes, because the statements demonstrate that the building inspector has an attitude toward a certain class of persons that interferes with the proper performance of the obligations of his job."
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0001.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body{\n      margin:0;\n      font-size:1rem;\n      line-height:1.7;\n      background:#ffffff;\n      color:#1f1f1f;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation{\n      padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing:border-box;\n      max-width:100%;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation p{\n      margin:0 0 1rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-center{\n      text-align:center;\n    }\n    .pbx-title{\n      font-size:1.5rem;\n      font-weight:700;\n      margin:0 0 1.2rem 0;\n      text-align:center;\n      line-height:1.25;\n    }\n    .pbx-figure{\n      width:100%;\n      display:flex;\n      justify-content:center;\n      margin:0.5rem 0 1.25rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-figure img{\n      max-width:100%;\n      height:auto;\n      display:block;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective{\n      background:#f0f7ff;\n      border-left:4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius:6px;\n      padding:14px 18px;\n      margin:24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title{\n      font-size:13px;\n      font-weight:700;\n      color:#2980b9;\n      text-transform:uppercase;\n      letter-spacing:0.05em;\n      margin-bottom:8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references{\n      background:#fafafa;\n      border:1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius:6px;\n      padding:14px 18px;\n      margin:20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title{\n      font-size:13px;\n      font-weight:700;\n      color:#555;\n      text-transform:uppercase;\n      letter-spacing:0.05em;\n      margin-bottom:8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list{\n      margin:0;\n      padding-left:18px;\n      font-size:14px;\n      color:#555;\n      line-height:1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-foot{\n      margin-top:1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-choice{\n      margin:0 0 0.9rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-choice strong{\n      font-weight:700;\n    }\n    @media (max-width:640px){\n      body{\n        font-size:0.95rem;\n        padding:0.75rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-explanation{\n        padding:0.875rem 1rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-title{\n        font-size:1.25rem;\n      }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Regulation of speech -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <div class=\"pbx-figure\" aria-label=\"Regulating private speech by public employee diagram\">\n    <img alt=\"Regulating private speech by public employee\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" />\n  </div>\n\n  <p>Acceptance of <strong>public employment</strong> does not eliminate an individual's <strong>right to free speech</strong>—but this right is <strong>not absolute</strong>. When a public employee is <strong>speaking as a private citizen</strong>, the government can limit that speech if its <strong>interest in efficient government function outweighs</strong> the employee's right to free speech. And when the employee is speaking pursuant to official duties (ie, within the scope of employment), the government has even greater latitude to regulate that speech and First Amendment protections rarely apply.</p>\n\n  <p>Here, the city building inspector was likely speaking as a private citizen since talking to a reporter presumably fell outside his official duties. But since the inspector's statements showed his lack of effort to get some buildings up to code, the city council's interest in ensuring that he properly perform his job outweighed his right to free speech. And if talking to reporters was an official duty, the city council's right to regulate that speech was even greater. Therefore, the city's decision to discharge him was constitutional.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice A)</strong> Comments on a matter of <em>public concern</em> (as seen here) are afforded greater First Amendment protection than those involving a <em>private</em> concern. But the city council still had \"good cause\" to fire the inspector since his statements demonstrated that he could not properly perform his job.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice B)</strong> The First Amendment (applied to the states through the Fourteenth Amendment) gives the media the right to publish information on matters of public concern. But the fact that the inspector's statements were published in a newspaper is irrelevant to determining whether the city council can fire him for those statements.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"C\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice C)</strong> A government employee can make public comments that are inconsistent with current government policy if those comments do not interfere with his/her ability to adequately perform official duties.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n    <p>When a public employee is speaking as a private citizen, the government can only restrict that speech if its interest in efficient government function outweighs the employee's right to free speech. But when the employee is speaking pursuant to official duties, the government has greater latitude to regulate that speech.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n    <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n      <li>Pickering v. Bd. of Educ., 391 U.S. 563, 568 (1968) (explaining that a public employee's right to free speech as a private citizen must be balanced against the government's interest in efficient government function).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一项城市法令规定，城市建筑监察员负责确保该市所有建筑都符合建筑规范标准，并要求监察员将所有已知的建筑规范违规行为移交起诉。另一项法令规定，城市建筑监察员可因“正当理由”被解雇。该建筑监察员带领一名报社记者参观了贫民区的一些破旧建筑。在用各种侮辱性绰号和诽谤言辞形容这些建筑的居住者后，该建筑监察员向记者表示：“我根本不打算让这些建筑达到规范标准，也不打算让它们的业主因违反规范而受到起诉，因为如果这些建筑被修复，住在里面的人只会再次破坏它们。”记者在当地报纸的一篇报道中发表了这些言论。该建筑监察员承认他发表了这些言论。\n\n基于这些言论，市议会解雇了该建筑监察员。\n\n市议会的行为是否合宪？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不合宪，因为这些言论是对公众关切事务的合法评论。",
        "B": "不合宪，因为这些言论发表在受 First and Fourteenth Amendments 保护的报纸上。",
        "C": "合宪，因为该建筑监察员是政府雇员，担任此类职位的人不得发表与现行政府政策不一致的公开评论。",
        "D": "合宪，因为这些言论表明该建筑监察员对某一类人群的态度妨碍了其正常履行工作职责。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f6f8;\r\n            color: #333;\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            background: #ffffff;\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n        .header {\r\n            background: #2c3e50;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .header h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n        .header .sub-title {\r\n            font-size: 12px;\r\n            opacity: 0.8;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n            text-transform: uppercase;\r\n            letter-spacing: 1px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-section {\r\n            background: #e8f5e9;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid #4caf50;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-label {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #2e7d32;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-text {\r\n            font-size: 18px;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 0 20px 20px 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-card {\r\n            background: #fff;\r\n            border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #1976d2;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-title::before {\r\n            content: \"⚖️\";\r\n            margin-right: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            padding: 2px 4px;\r\n            border-radius: 3px;\r\n            font-weight: 500;\r\n        }\r\n        .case-ref {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #555;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n            border-bottom: 1px dashed #999;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong-option {\r\n            margin-top: 10px;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            background-color: #fafafa;\r\n            border-left: 3px solid #bdbdbd;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #757575;\r\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n        .mbe-tip {\r\n            background: #e3f2fd;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            border: 1px solid #bbdefb;\r\n        }\r\n        .mbe-tip-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #0d47a1;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <div class=\"sub-title\">Constitutional Law / First Amendment</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"answer-section\">\r\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">正确答案</div>\r\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">选项 D (Yes)</div>\r\n        <div style=\"font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 5px; color: #555;\">\r\n            合宪，因为言论表明其态度妨碍了工作职责的履行。\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 核心考点 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\">核心考点：公职人员言论自由</div>\r\n            <p>本题考察的是政府雇员（Public Employee）的言论自由权与政府作为雇主维持高效运作（Efficient Government Function）之间的平衡。</p>\r\n            <p>适用的法律标准通常被称为 <b>Pickering Balancing Test</b>（皮克林平衡测试）：</p>\r\n            <ol style=\"padding-left: 20px; margin: 10px 0;\">\r\n                <li><b>第一步：</b>雇员是否就“公众关切的事项”（Matter of Public Concern）发言？</li>\r\n                <li><b>第二步：</b>如果是，法院必须权衡雇员的言论利益与政府促进公共服务效率的利益。</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 案情分析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\" style=\"border-left: 4px solid #1976d2;\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\">本题逻辑分析</div>\r\n            <p>虽然建筑监察员谈论的是贫民窟建筑状况（属于公众关切事项），但他的言论内容不仅是观点表达，更是<b>承认了渎职</b>。</p>\r\n            <p>他明确表示：“我根本不打算让这些建筑达到规范标准...”（I do not even try...）。</p>\r\n            <p><b>关键点：</b>当言论直接证明雇员拒绝履行核心职责（Insubordination or neglect of duty）时，政府维持机构正常运作的利益<b>压倒</b>了雇员的言论自由权。</p>\r\n            <p>因此，市议会有“正当理由”（Good Cause）解雇他，这不违反宪法。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 错误选项解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\">为什么其他选项是错的？</div>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n                <div class=\"wrong-title\">选项 A：错误</div>\r\n                虽然言论确实涉及“公众关切”，但这并不是绝对的护身符。如果言论本身证明了雇员不称职（Incompetence），政府仍可解雇他。\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n                <div class=\"wrong-title\">选项 B：错误</div>\r\n                媒体发布（Published in a newspaper）并不改变雇佣关系的本质。First Amendment 保护报纸发布的权利，但不豁免雇员因承认渎职而承担的后果。\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n                <div class=\"wrong-title\">选项 C：错误</div>\r\n                这个选项太绝对了。公职人员<b>可以</b>批评政府政策（例如：“我认为这个建筑法规不合理”），只要这种批评不导致工作场所的混乱或妨碍履职。本题的关键在于他<b>拒绝执行</b>政策，而不仅仅是口头反对。\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        <div class=\"mbe-tip\">\r\n            <div class=\"mbe-tip-title\">💡 MBE 考试技巧</div>\r\n            <p>在处理 <b>Public Employee Speech</b> 问题时，请遵循以下思维路径：</p>\r\n            <ol style=\"padding-left: 20px; margin: 5px 0;\">\r\n                <li>如果是履行职务时的发言（Official Duties）👉 <b>无</b> First Amendment 保护（政府可随意监管）。</li>\r\n                <li>如果是作为公民发言（Citizen）：\r\n                    <ul style=\"padding-left: 15px; margin: 5px 0;\">\r\n                        <li>看是否干扰了工作（Disruption/Interference）。</li>\r\n                        <li>本题中，\"I do not even try\" = 承认不工作 = <b>极大的干扰</b>。</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n                </li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
      "meta": {
