    {
      "index": 5,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Regulation of speech",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "In an effort to prevent quid pro quo corruption between donors and candidates for state elective office, a state enacted a law that limits the total amount an individual may contribute to individual candidates during an election cycle. A donor who was fined for violating this statute has argued that it is unconstitutional.\nIs the state law constitutional?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because political speech cannot be restricted.",
        "B": "No, because the law is not the least restrictive means to serve a compelling state interest.",
        "C": "Yes, because campaign contributions are not speech protected by the First Amendment.",
        "D": "Yes, because the law is closely drawn to serve an important state interest."
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0005.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      color: #111;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation {\n      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      max-width: 100%;\n      overflow-wrap: break-word;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n    .pbx-tab {\n      display: inline-block;\n      border: 1px solid #d9d9d9;\n      border-bottom: none;\n      border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0;\n      padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;\n      font-size: 1.05rem;\n      margin-left: 0.25rem;\n      margin-top: 0.2rem;\n      background: #fff;\n    }\n    .pbx-divider {\n      height: 1px;\n      background: #d9d9d9;\n      margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-scroll-x {\n      overflow-x: auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;\n      margin: 1rem 0;\n    }\n    table.pbx-table {\n      width: 100%;\n      min-width: 48rem;\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n      table-layout: fixed;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-table th, .pbx-table td {\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n      padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;\n      vertical-align: top;\n      text-align: left;\n      word-break: break-word;\n      overflow-wrap: break-word;\n    }\n    .pbx-table th {\n      background: #f5f5f5;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-table .pbx-lefthead {\n      width: 16%;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      font-size: 1.05rem;\n      vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n    .pbx-table ul {\n      margin: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 1.2rem;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-table li {\n      margin: 0.15rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-note {\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n      margin-top: 0.75rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-note p {\n      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding-left: 18px;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      color: #555;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body {\n        font-size: 0.95rem;\n        padding: 0.75rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-explanation {\n        padding: 0.875rem 1rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-tab {\n        font-size: 1rem;\n        padding: 0.65rem 1.1rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-table th, .pbx-table td {\n        font-size: 0.825rem;\n        padding: 0.5em 0.625em;\n      }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Regulation of speech -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <div class=\"pbx-tab\">Explanation</div>\n  <div class=\"pbx-divider\"></div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-scroll-x\">\n    <table class=\"pbx-table\" aria-label=\"Campaign-finance restrictions\">\n      <tr>\n        <th colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size:1.15rem;\">Campaign-finance restrictions</th>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th style=\"width:18%;\"></th>\n        <th>Examples</th>\n        <th>Test</th>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td class=\"pbx-lefthead\">Contribution<br>restrictions</td>\n        <td>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Limit on amount of contribution to:\n              <ul>\n                <li>single candidate</li>\n                <li>political candidates, parties &amp; action committees combined</li>\n              </ul>\n            </li>\n            <li>Increase of limit on amount of contribution to candidate when self-financed opponent exceeds certain spending amount</li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n        <td>\n          <div>Intermediate scrutiny</div>\n          <ul>\n            <li>closely drawn/substantially related to important government interest</li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td class=\"pbx-lefthead\">Expenditure<br>restrictions</td>\n        <td>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Limit on spending by:\n              <ul>\n                <li>corporations or unions in support of or opposition to candidate</li>\n                <li>candidate on his/her own behalf</li>\n              </ul>\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n        <td>\n          <div>Strict scrutiny</div>\n          <ul>\n            <li>necessary/least restrictive means to achieve compelling government interest</li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-note\">\n    <p>The First Amendment protects political speech, which includes campaign contributions and expenditures <strong>(Choice C)</strong>. Political speech is fundamental to a free and democratic society but may be restricted if the government satisfies the appropriate level of scrutiny <strong>(Choice A)</strong>. A government restriction on campaign contributions must survive intermediate scrutiny, which requires the government to prove that its restriction is closely drawn to serve (ie, substantially related to) an important government interest.</p>\n\n    <p>Here, the state law limits the amount that an individual may contribute to a single candidate for state elective office during an election cycle. The state has an important interest in preventing quid pro quo corruption between donors and candidates.* And in <em>Buckley v. Valeo</em>, the U.S. Supreme Court held that limiting the amount of money an individual may donate to a single candidate is closely drawn to serve that interest. Therefore, the state law is constitutional.</p>\n\n    <p><em>*Preventing quid pro quo corruption or the appearance of it is the only government interest that the U.S. Supreme Court has recognized is important enough to justify government restrictions on campaign contributions.</em></p>\n\n    <p><strong>(Choice B)</strong> A government restriction on campaign expenditures must satisfy strict scrutiny—ie, the government must show that its restriction is the least restrictive means to serve a compelling government interest. However, this law restricts campaign contributions, so the state need only satisfy intermediate scrutiny.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n    <p>The First Amendment protects political speech, which includes campaign contributions and expenditures. A law that restricts campaign contributions is unconstitutional unless the government satisfies intermediate scrutiny by showing that the law is closely drawn to serve (ie, substantially related to) an important government interest.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n    <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n      <li>Buckley v. Valeo, 424 U.S. 1, 29 (1976) (holding that a limit on the amount an individual may donate to a candidate is a constitutional means to serve the government's important interest in combating quid pro quo corruption).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "为防止州民选公职的捐赠者与候选人之间发生交换条件式腐败，某州颁布了一项法律，限制个人在选举周期内可向个别候选人捐赠的总金额。一名因违反该法规而被罚款的捐赠者主张，该法规违宪。\n\n该州法律是否合宪？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "否，因为政治言论不能被限制。",
        "B": "否，因为该法律并非为达成一项迫切的州利益而采取的限制性最小的手段。",
        "C": "是，因为竞选捐款并非受First Amendment保护的言论。",
        "D": "是，因为该法律是为服务于一项重要的州利益而紧密拟定的。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n\r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n    body {\r\n        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n        background-color: #f4f6f8;\r\n        color: #333;\r\n        line-height: 1.6;\r\n        margin: 0;\r\n        padding: 10px;\r\n        display: flex;\r\n        justify-content: center;\r\n    }\r\n    .container {\r\n        max-width: 480px;\r\n        background: #ffffff;\r\n        border-radius: 12px;\r\n        box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n        overflow: hidden;\r\n    }\r\n    .header {\r\n        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2c3e50, #4ca1af);\r\n        color: white;\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n        text-align: center;\r\n    }\r\n    .header h1 {\r\n        margin: 0;\r\n        font-size: 20px;\r\n        font-weight: 700;\r\n    }\r\n    .header p {\r\n        margin: 5px 0 0;\r\n        font-size: 14px;\r\n        opacity: 0.9;\r\n    }\r\n    .content {\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n    .answer-box {\r\n        background-color: #e8f5e9;\r\n        border-left: 5px solid #4caf50;\r\n        padding: 15px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        border-radius: 4px;\r\n    }\r\n    .answer-title {\r\n        color: #2e7d32;\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n        font-size: 16px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n    }\r\n    .section-title {\r\n        font-size: 18px;\r\n        font-weight: 600;\r\n        color: #2c3e50;\r\n        margin-top: 20px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n        border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;\r\n        padding-bottom: 5px;\r\n    }\r\n    .concept-card {\r\n        background: #f8f9fa;\r\n        border: 1px solid #e9ecef;\r\n        border-radius: 8px;\r\n        padding: 15px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n    }\r\n    .comparison-table {\r\n        width: 100%;\r\n        border-collapse: collapse;\r\n        margin: 15px 0;\r\n        font-size: 14px;\r\n    }\r\n    .comparison-table th, .comparison-table td {\r\n        border: 1px solid #ddd;\r\n        padding: 8px;\r\n        text-align: left;\r\n    }\r\n    .comparison-table th {\r\n        background-color: #f2f2f2;\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n    }\r\n    .highlight {\r\n        background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n        padding: 2px 4px;\r\n        border-radius: 3px;\r\n        font-weight: 500;\r\n    }\r\n    .case-ref {\r\n        font-style: italic;\r\n        color: #555;\r\n        font-size: 0.9em;\r\n    }\r\n    .exam-tip {\r\n        background-color: #fff8e1;\r\n        border: 1px dashed #ffc107;\r\n        padding: 15px;\r\n        border-radius: 8px;\r\n        margin-top: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n    .exam-tip-title {\r\n        color: #ff8f00;\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n        margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        display: flex;\r\n        align-items: center;\r\n    }\r\n    .icon {\r\n        margin-right: 5px;\r\n    }\r\n    .wrong-option {\r\n        color: #c62828;\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n    }\r\n</style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <p>宪法：竞选资金与言论自由</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 正确答案部分 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n            <div class=\"answer-title\">✅ 正确答案：D</div>\r\n            <p>是的，因为该法律是为服务于一项重要的州利益而紧密拟定的 (Closely drawn to serve an important state interest)。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 核心法律规则 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">⚖️ 核心法律规则</div>\r\n        <p>本题的核心在于区分<b>竞选捐款 (Campaign Contributions)</b> 和 <b>竞选支出 (Campaign Expenditures)</b> 的审查标准。</p>\r\n        \r\n        <p>根据美国最高法院在 <span class=\"case-ref\">Buckley v. Valeo (1976)</span> 中的裁定：</p>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <table class=\"comparison-table\">\r\n                <thead>\r\n                    <tr>\r\n                        <th>类型</th>\r\n                        <th>审查标准 (Scrutiny)</th>\r\n                        <th>合宪性</th>\r\n                    </tr>\r\n                </thead>\r\n                <tbody>\r\n                    <tr>\r\n                        <td><b>捐款限制</b><br>(Contributions)</td>\r\n                        <td><b>中度审查 / 紧密拟定</b><br>(Intermediate / Closely Drawn)</td>\r\n                        <td>通常<b>合宪</b><br>(如果为了防止腐败)</td>\r\n                    </tr>\r\n                    <tr>\r\n                        <td><b>支出限制</b><br>(Expenditures)</td>\r\n                        <td><b>严格审查</b><br>(Strict Scrutiny)</td>\r\n                        <td>通常<b>违宪</b><br>(很难满足标准)</td>\r\n                    </tr>\r\n                </tbody>\r\n            </table>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 深度解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">🔍 深度解析</div>\r\n        <p><b>1. 为什么是“紧密拟定” (Closely Drawn)？</b></p>\r\n        <p>法院认为，限制一个人给候选人捐多少钱，对言论自由的限制相对较小（只是限制了表达支持的“音量”，而不是禁止表达支持本身）。因此，政府不需要证明这是“限制最小的手段” (Least restrictive means)，只需要证明该法律与<b>重要的政府利益 (Important government interest)</b> 密切相关。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>2. 什么是“重要的政府利益”？</b></p>\r\n        <p>在本案中，防止<b>“交换条件式腐败” (Quid pro quo corruption)</b> 或其表象，被法院认定为足够重要的利益，可以正当化对捐款的限制。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>3. 结合题目：</b></p>\r\n        <p>题目中该州法律限制的是<b>“个人捐赠的总金额” (Contribution)</b>。因此，适用中度审查（Closely Drawn）。选项 D 准确地复述了这一法律标准。</p>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 错误选项分析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">❌ 为什么其他选项错误？</div>\r\n        \r\n        <p><span class=\"wrong-option\">选项 A 错误：</span> 虽然政治言论受保护，但它不是绝对的。为了防止腐败，政府可以进行适当限制。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><span class=\"wrong-option\">选项 B 错误：</span> 这是一个典型的<b>陷阱选项</b>。它描述的是<b>严格审查 (Strict Scrutiny)</b> 的标准（\"least restrictive means\" + \"compelling interest\"）。严格审查适用于限制候选人花多少钱（支出），而不适用于限制捐赠者给多少钱（捐款）。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><span class=\"wrong-option\">选项 C 错误：</span> 竞选捐款<b>确实</b>属于受第一修正案保护的言论形式（Money is speech），只是受保护程度不如直接的政治演说高，因此可以受到更严格的监管，但不能说它完全不受保护。</p>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        <div class=\"exam-tip\">\r\n            <div class=\"exam-tip-title\">💡 MBE 考试技巧</div>\r\n            <p>在遇到竞选资金 (Campaign Finance) 的题目时，第一步先判断限制的对象：</p>\r\n            <ul>\r\n                <li>如果是限制<b>给钱 (Giving/Contribution)</b> ➡️ 标准较低 ➡️ 法律通常<b>有效</b>。</li>\r\n                <li>如果是限制<b>花钱 (Spending/Expenditure)</b> ➡️ 标准极高 ➡️ 法律通常<b>无效</b>。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n            <p>记住口诀：<b>\"You can limit the giving, but you can't limit the spending.\"</b></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
