    {
      "index": 7,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Procedural Due Process Applied",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A doctor who was licensed to practice medicine in a particular state was convicted in state court of improperly distributing specified drugs by writing prescriptions for fictitious persons. Under state law, such an abuse of the prescription-writing privilege requires revocation of a doctor's license. After it received an official notification of the doctor's conviction, the state medical board revoked the doctor's license without affording him any opportunity for a hearing.\nThe doctor has sued the board in state court to set aside the revocation, alleging deprivation of property without due process of law because the board did not provide an opportunity for a trial-type hearing before revoking the license. The doctor does not deny the conviction or the factual basis for it.\nWhich of the following is the strongest argument in support of the state medical board?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "A doctor's license to practice is a privilege, not a right, and therefore is not property within the meaning of the due process clause of the Fourteenth Amendment.",
        "B": "Due process requires a balancing of interests, and the state's interest in preventing drug abuse outweighs the doctor's interest in the particular procedure followed in the disciplinary proceeding.",
        "C": "The adjudicative facts necessary to revoke the doctor's license were determined in the criminal trial, and therefore due process does not require any further trial-type hearing.",
        "D": "The licensing board was required to summarily revoke the doctor's license because Article IV, Section 1, of the Constitution requires the licensing board to give full faith and credit to the doctor's criminal conviction."
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0007.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body{\n      margin:0;\n      font-size:1rem;\n      line-height:1.7;\n      background:#fff;\n      color:#111;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation{\n      padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      max-width: 100%;\n      box-sizing:border-box;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation p{\n      margin:0 0 1rem 0;\n      word-break: break-word;\n      overflow-wrap: break-word;\n    }\n    .pbx-title{\n      text-align:center;\n      font-weight:700;\n      font-size:1.15rem;\n      line-height:1.25;\n      margin:1rem 0 1.5rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-title em{\n      font-style:italic;\n      font-weight:700;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-wrap{\n      margin: 0 auto 1.25rem;\n      width:100%;\n    }\n    .pbx-scroll-x{\n      overflow-x:auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;\n      margin:16px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-inner{\n      min-width: 760px;\n      position:relative;\n      padding: 0 0 1rem;\n      box-sizing:border-box;\n    }\n    .pbx-balance{\n      position:relative;\n      height: 260px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n    .pbx-bar{\n      position:absolute;\n      left:0;\n      right:0;\n      top:148px;\n      height:5px;\n      background:#646464;\n      border-radius:3px;\n    }\n    .pbx-stand{\n      position:absolute;\n      left:50%;\n      top:151px;\n      transform:translateX(-50%);\n      width:0;height:0;\n      border-left:58px solid transparent;\n      border-right:58px solid transparent;\n      border-top:116px solid #8a8f95;\n      filter: drop-shadow(10px 0 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.08));\n    }\n    .pbx-weight{\n      position:absolute;\n      width:108px;\n      height:92px;\n      background:linear-gradient(#8a8f95,#5f656b);\n      border-radius:10px 10px 12px 12px;\n      box-shadow: inset 0 -8px 18px rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\n    }\n    .pbx-weight:before{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      left:50%;\n      top:-10px;\n      transform:translateX(-50%);\n      width:26px;\n      height:26px;\n      border:8px solid #666b71;\n      border-bottom:none;\n      border-radius:18px 18px 0 0;\n      background:transparent;\n      box-sizing:border-box;\n    }\n    .pbx-weight:after{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      inset:18px 16px 16px;\n      border-radius:6px;\n      background:rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\n    }\n    .pbx-w-left{ left:74px; top:86px; transform:rotate(0deg); }\n    .pbx-w-mid{ left:50%; top:86px; transform:translateX(-50%); opacity:.86; }\n    .pbx-w-right{ right:74px; top:86px; transform:rotate(0deg); }\n    .pbx-arrow{\n      position:absolute;\n      top:132px;\n      width:54px;\n      height:16px;\n      border-top:3px solid #c7d6f3;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow:before{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      top:-7px;\n      width:12px;height:12px;\n      border-top:3px solid #c7d6f3;\n      border-right:3px solid #c7d6f3;\n      transform:rotate(45deg);\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-left{ left:300px; transform:scaleX(-1); }\n    .pbx-arrow-right{ right:300px; }\n    .pbx-label{\n      position:absolute;\n      top:12px;\n      width:210px;\n      text-align:center;\n      font-size:1.02rem;\n      line-height:1.25;\n      color:#333;\n    }\n    .pbx-label.mid{ left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%); top:10px; }\n    .pbx-label.left{ left:56px; }\n    .pbx-label.right{ right:56px; }\n    .pbx-caption{\n      position:absolute;\n      top: 196px;\n      width:260px;\n      text-align:center;\n      font-size:1rem;\n      color:#333;\n    }\n    .pbx-caption.left{ left:0; }\n    .pbx-caption.right{ right:0; }\n    .pbx-maintext{\n      margin-top: 0.5rem;\n      font-size:1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-maintext strong{ font-weight:700; }\n    .pbx-maintext .pbx-blue{ color:#1a73d9; }\n    .pbx-bullets{\n      margin:0.5rem 0 1.5rem 1.2rem;\n      padding-left:1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-bullets li{ margin:0.35rem 0; }\n    .pbx-choice{\n      margin: 0 0 0.8rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective{\n      background:#f0f7ff;\n      border-left:4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius:6px;\n      padding:14px 18px;\n      margin:24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title{\n      font-size:13px;\n      font-weight:700;\n      color:#2980b9;\n      text-transform:uppercase;\n      letter-spacing:0.05em;\n      margin-bottom:8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references{\n      background:#fafafa;\n      border:1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius:6px;\n      padding:14px 18px;\n      margin:20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title{\n      font-size:13px;\n      font-weight:700;\n      color:#555;\n      text-transform:uppercase;\n      letter-spacing:0.05em;\n      margin-bottom:8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list{\n      margin:0;\n      padding-left:18px;\n      font-size:14px;\n      color:#555;\n      line-height:1.7;\n    }\n    @media (max-width:640px){\n      body{ font-size:0.95rem; padding:0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation{ padding:0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-title{ font-size:1.05rem; }\n      .pbx-label{ font-size:.95rem; }\n      .pbx-caption{ font-size:.92rem; }\n      .pbx-maintext{ font-size:.95rem; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Procedural Due Process Applied -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <div class=\"pbx-title\">Procedural due process<br><em>(Mathews v. Eldridge balancing test)</em></div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-flow-wrap\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-scroll-x\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-flow-inner\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-balance\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-label left\">Private interest<br>affected by<br>deprivation</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-label mid\">Risk of erroneous<br>deprivation + Value<br>of other safeguards</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-label right\">Government interest<br>(administrative &amp;<br>fiscal burdens)</div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-weight pbx-w-left\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-weight pbx-w-mid\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-weight pbx-w-right\"></div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-arrow pbx-arrow-left\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-arrow pbx-arrow-right\"></div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-bar\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-stand\"></div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-caption left\">Insufficient process</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-caption right\">Sufficient process</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-maintext\"><strong>Procedural due process</strong> requires that the government provide <strong>reasonable notice</strong> and a <strong>meaningful opportunity to be heard</strong> before a neutral decision-maker when depriving persons of <span class=\"pbx-blue\">life, liberty, or property</span>. To determine whether the government provided due process, courts <strong>balance three factors</strong>:</p>\n\n  <ul class=\"pbx-bullets\">\n    <li>the <strong>private interest</strong> affected by the deprivation</li>\n    <li>the <strong>risk of erroneous deprivation</strong> of that interest through current procedures and the probable <strong>value of additional or substitute procedural safeguards</strong> and</li>\n    <li>the <strong>government's interest</strong>, including the fiscal and administrative burdens that other safeguards would entail.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-maintext\">Here, the doctor's property interest in his medical license is likely outweighed by the state's interest in preventing drug abuse—particularly since additional or substitute proceedings would fiscally and administratively burden the medical board. And the risk of erroneously depriving the doctor of his license is low given the protections afforded in his related criminal proceeding. Therefore, the board's strongest argument is that the facts necessary to revoke the doctor's license were determined in the criminal trial, so no further trial-type hearing is required.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice A)</strong> Due process protections historically extended to rights—not privileges. But this distinction has been abandoned, and such protections extend to any legitimate life, liberty, or property interest.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice B)</strong> Due process does require a balancing of interests. But it weighs the state's interest in preventing drug abuse against the doctor's interest in his license (not the board's particular procedures) and the risks of current procedures and value of alternative safeguards.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"D\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice D)</strong> Under the full faith and credit clause, a valid judgment issued in one state must be recognized in every other state. This clause does not apply here since the doctor's conviction and license revocation occurred in the same state. But even if it did, the state need only honor the criminal conviction—not revoke the doctor's license.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n    <p>Procedural due process is assessed by weighing three factors: (1) the private interest affected, (2) the risk of erroneous deprivation of that interest and probable value of other procedural safeguards, and (3) the government's interest, including the fiscal and administrative burdens that other safeguards would entail.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n    <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n      <li>Mathews v. Eldridge, 424 U.S. 319, 335 (1976) (listing the three factors used to assess compliance with procedural due process).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一名在某州获得行医执照的医生，因给虚构人物开具处方，不当分发特定药物而被州法院定罪。根据州法律，滥用处方权的此种行为需要吊销医生的执照。州医疗委员会在收到该医生被定罪的正式通知后，未经听证程序即吊销了该医生的执照。<br><br>该医生已向州法院起诉该委员会，要求撤销吊销决定，声称委员会在吊销其执照前未提供审判式听证的机会，侵犯了其未经正当法律程序而被剥夺财产的权利。该医生并未否认其定罪或其事实依据。<br><br>以下哪项是支持州医疗委员会的最有力论点？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "医生的行医执照是一种特权，而非权利，因此不属于《第十四修正案》正当程序条款所指的财产。",
        "B": "正当程序要求利益衡量，而州在防止药物滥用方面的利益，重于医生在纪律处分程序中所遵循的特定程序中的利益。",
        "C": "吊销医生执照所需的裁决性事实已在刑事审判中确定，因此正当程序不要求任何进一步的审判式听证。",
        "D": "执照委员会被要求立即吊销医生的执照，因为《宪法》第四条第一款要求执照委员会对医生的刑事定罪给予充分信任和尊重。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #e8f4f8;\r\n            --correct-bg: #d4edda;\r\n            --correct-text: #155724;\r\n            --wrong-bg: #f8d7da;\r\n            --wrong-text: #721c24;\r\n            --text-color: #333;\r\n            --card-bg: #ffffff;\r\n        }\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f4f4;\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            background: var(--card-bg);\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n        .header {\r\n            background: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .header h2 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n        .header .sub-title {\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-box {\r\n            background: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            border-left: 5px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\r\n            display: block;\r\n        }\r\n        .analysis-section {\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .choice-analysis {\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n            padding: 12px;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        .correct {\r\n            background-color: var(--correct-bg);\r\n            color: var(--correct-text);\r\n            border: 1px solid #c3e6cb;\r\n        }\r\n        .trap {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            color: #856404;\r\n            border: 1px solid #ffeeba;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong {\r\n            background-color: var(--wrong-bg);\r\n            color: var(--wrong-text);\r\n            border: 1px solid #f5c6cb;\r\n        }\r\n        .badge {\r\n            display: inline-block;\r\n            padding: 2px 6px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n            font-size: 0.75rem;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-right: 5px;\r\n            text-transform: uppercase;\r\n        }\r\n        .badge-correct { background: #28a745; color: white; }\r\n        .badge-trap { background: #ffc107; color: black; }\r\n        .badge-wrong { background: #dc3545; color: white; }\r\n        \r\n        .key-point {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            text-decoration: underline;\r\n            text-decoration-color: var(--accent-color);\r\n        }\r\n        .latin {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #555;\r\n        }\r\n        .footer-tip {\r\n            background: #333;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            border-bottom-left-radius: 12px;\r\n            border-bottom-right-radius: 12px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n    <title>MBE Question Analysis</title>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h2>MBE 考点解析</h2>\r\n        <div class=\"sub-title\">Constitutional Law: Procedural Due Process</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 核心考点讲解 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-box\">\r\n            <span class=\"concept-title\">⚖️ 核心考点：Mathews v. Eldridge 测试</span>\r\n            <p>在决定政府剥夺个人财产（如执照）前需要何种程序时，法院使用三要素平衡测试：</p>\r\n            <ol style=\"padding-left: 20px; margin: 5px 0;\">\r\n                <li><b>私人利益</b> (Private Interest)：被剥夺权益的重要性。</li>\r\n                <li><b>错误风险</b> (Risk of Error)：现有程序的出错概率及额外程序的价值。</li>\r\n                <li><b>政府利益</b> (Government Interest)：行政效率和财政负担。</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 正确答案解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"analysis-section\">\r\n            <h3 style=\"color: var(--primary-color); border-bottom: 2px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 5px;\">✅ 为什么选 C？</h3>\r\n            <div class=\"choice-analysis correct\">\r\n                <span class=\"badge badge-correct\">正确答案</span>\r\n                <strong>裁决性事实已在刑事审判中确定</strong>\r\n                <p>本题的关键在于 <span class=\"latin\">Mathews</span> 测试的第二个要素：<b>额外程序的价值</b>。</p>\r\n                <p>医生已经被刑事法庭定罪。刑事审判的证明标准是“排除合理怀疑” (Beyond a reasonable doubt)，这是最高的证明标准。既然事实已经在刑事法庭上被严格证实，那么在行政听证会上再次确认这些事实（通常仅需“优势证据”标准）是<b>毫无必要的重复</b>。</p>\r\n                <p>因此，在此情境下，举行听证会来确认“医生是否开了假处方”这一事实，其<b>错误剥夺的风险几乎为零</b>，额外听证会的价值也为零。</p>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 干扰项解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"analysis-section\">\r\n            <h3 style=\"color: var(--primary-color); border-bottom: 2px solid #eee; padding-bottom: 5px;\">❌ 为什么其他选项错误？</h3>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"choice-analysis trap\">\r\n                <span class=\"badge badge-trap\">高频陷阱</span>\r\n                <strong>选项 B：利益衡量 (Balancing of Interests)</strong>\r\n                <p>这是一个精心设计的干扰项。虽然正当程序确实涉及“利益衡量”，但选项 B 的表述是错误的。</p>\r\n                <p>它错误地将“政府防止药物滥用的宏观利益”与“医生对特定程序的微观利益”进行对比。真正的 <span class=\"latin\">Mathews</span> 测试衡量的是：<b>增加额外程序的行政负担</b> vs. <b>该程序减少错误判决的价值</b>。选项 B 忽略了本案中“事实已被刑事定罪确认”这一核心逻辑。</p>\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"choice-analysis wrong\">\r\n                <span class=\"badge badge-wrong\">错误观念</span>\r\n                <strong>选项 A：权利 vs. 特权 (Right vs. Privilege)</strong>\r\n                <p>这是一个过时的法律概念。现代宪法学（自 <span class=\"latin\">Goldberg v. Kelly</span> 等案以来）已经废弃了“权利与特权”的区别。职业执照被视为受第十四修正案保护的<b>财产利益 (Property Interest)</b>。</p>\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"choice-analysis wrong\">\r\n                <span class=\"badge badge-wrong\">适用错误</span>\r\n                <strong>选项 D：充分信任和尊重 (Full Faith and Credit)</strong>\r\n                <p>该条款 (Article IV, Section 1) 主要适用于<b>州与州之间</b>承认判决。本案是<b>同一个州</b>内部的刑事法院和行政机构之间的关系，因此该条款不适用。</p>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"footer-tip\">\r\n        💡 <b>MBE 解题技巧：</b><br>\r\n        当题目涉及“基于刑事定罪的行政处罚”时，通常不需要新的事实听证会。因为刑事定罪提供了最高级别的程序保护，这本身就满足了 Due Process 对事实认定的要求。\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
      "meta": {
        "question_analysis": {
