    {
      "index": 8,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Types Of Taking",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A purchaser bought land in the mountain foothills just outside a resort town and planned to build a housing development there. Soon thereafter, the county in which the land was located unexpectedly adopted a regulation that, for the first time, prohibited all construction in several foothill and mountain areas, including the area of the purchaser's property. The purpose of the county's regulation was \"to conserve for future generations the unique natural wildlife and plant habitats\" in the mountain areas. Since the adoption of the regulation, the purchaser has been unable to lease or sell the property at any price. Several realtors have advised the purchaser that his property is now worthless.\nThe purchaser has sued the county, claiming that the regulation has effected a taking of the purchaser's property and that the county therefore owes the purchaser just compensation.\nIs the court likely to rule in favor of the purchaser?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because the county did not take title to the property from the purchaser.",
        "B": "No, because the regulation has not caused or authorized any uninvited physical invasion or intrusion onto the property.",
        "C": "Yes, because the conservation objective of the county ordinance is not sufficiently compelling to justify the substantial diminution in the property value.",
        "D": "Yes, because the effect of the county's regulation is to deny the purchaser's investment-backed expectation and essentially all economically beneficial use of the property."
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0008.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n      background: #fff;\n      color: #111;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation {\n      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      max-width: 100%;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation * {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation p {\n      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-scroll-x {\n      overflow-x: auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;\n      margin: 1rem 0;\n    }\n    table {\n      min-width: 480px;\n      width: 100%;\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n    }\n    th, td {\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n      padding: 8px 12px;\n      vertical-align: top;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      text-align: left;\n    }\n    th {\n      background: #f5f5f5;\n      font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    .pbx-title {\n      text-align: center;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      font-size: 1.15rem;\n      padding: 0.5rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-table-title {\n      text-align: center;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      font-size: 1.15rem;\n    }\n    ul {\n      margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem 1.25rem;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n    li {\n      margin: 0.15rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding-left: 18px;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      color: #555;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-footnote {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #666;\n      font-size: 0.95rem;\n      margin-top: 0.75rem;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation { padding: 0.875rem 1rem; }\n      th, td { font-size: 0.825rem; padding: 0.5em 0.625em; }\n      .pbx-table-title { font-size: 1rem; }\n      .pbx-edu-objective-title, .pbx-references-title { font-size: 13px; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- pbx-topic: Types Of Taking -->\n  <div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-scroll-x\">\n      <table>\n        <tr>\n          <th colspan=\"2\" class=\"pbx-table-title\">Fifth Amendment takings</th>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <th style=\"width: 21%;\">Type</th>\n          <th>Attributes</th>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td><strong>Physical</strong></td>\n          <td>• Possession or permanent physical invasion of property</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td><strong>Regulatory</strong></td>\n          <td>\n            • Deprivation of all economically beneficial uses<br>\n            • Restricts use under totality of circumstances:<br>\n            ◦ character of government action<br>\n            ◦ economic impact<br>\n            ◦ reasonable investment-back expectations\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td><strong>Exaction</strong></td>\n          <td>• Condition to obtain building/development permit</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td><strong>Destruction</strong></td>\n          <td>• Destruction of property or property interest (eg, easements, liens)</td>\n        </tr>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n\n    <p><strong>A taking</strong> occurs when the government:</p>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>physically possesses or invades private property</strong> (ie, physical taking) or</li>\n      <li><strong>deprives</strong> the owner of <strong>all economically beneficial use</strong> of the property <strong>but the owner retains possession</strong> (ie, regulatory taking) <strong>(Choices A &amp; B)</strong>.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <p>And under the Fifth Amendment—as applied to the states through the Fourteenth Amendment—a taking must be for a public use, and the government must justly compensate the owner for the property's fair market value.</p>\n\n    <p>Here, the county's regulation prohibits all construction on the purchaser's land. This amounted to a regulatory taking because it denied the purchaser (1) his investment-backed expectation for the planned housing development and (2) essentially all economically beneficial use of the property. And since the property was rendered worthless, the court will likely rule that the purchaser is entitled to just compensation.</p>\n\n    <p data-choice=\"C\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong>(Choice C)</strong> The ordinance's objective to conserve natural wildlife and plant habitats may be compelling. But the county can only justify the substantial diminution in the purchaser's property value by providing him just compensation.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n      <p>A Fifth Amendment taking occurs when (1) the government physically possesses or invades private property or (2) the owner retains possession but loses all economically beneficial use of the property due to government action.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n      <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n        <li>Lucas v. S.C. Coastal Council, 505 U.S. 1003, 1019 (1992) (holding that a deprivation of all economically beneficial uses of property constitutes a taking).</li>\n        <li>26 Am Jur. 2d Eminent Domain § 12 (2019) (explaining a deprivation of all economically beneficial uses of property).</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一名购买者在一个度假小镇外的山麓地带购买了土地，并计划在那里建造一个住宅开发项目。此后不久，该土地所在的县出人意料地通过了一项法规，首次禁止在包括购买者财产所在区域在内的几个山麓和山区进行所有建设。该县法规的目的是“为后代保护山区独特的自然野生动植物栖息地”。自该法规通过以来，购买者一直无法以任何价格出租或出售该房产。几位房地产经纪人已告知购买者，他的财产现在一文不值。\n\n购买者已起诉该县，声称该法规构成了对其财产的征收，因此该县应向购买者支付公正补偿。\n\n法院是否可能作出有利于购买者的裁决？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不会，因为该县并未从购买者手中取得该财产的所有权。",
        "B": "不会，因为该法规并未导致或授权任何未经邀请的对该财产的物理侵占或侵入。",
        "C": "会，因为该县法令的保护目标不足以成为财产价值大幅减损的正当理由。",
        "D": "会，因为该县法规的效果是剥夺了购买者有投资支持的预期，以及该财产基本上所有的经济上有利的用途。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #e8f4f8;\r\n            --text-color: #333;\r\n            --card-bg: #ffffff;\r\n            --border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            background-color: #f4f7f6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            width: 100%;\r\n            background: transparent;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .card {\r\n            background: var(--card-bg);\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        h1 {\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            margin-top: 0;\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        h2 {\r\n            font-size: 16px;\r\n            color: var(--accent-color);\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            text-transform: uppercase;\r\n            letter-spacing: 1px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        p {\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n            font-size: 15px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            padding: 2px 5px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #2980b9;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .english-term {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .case-box {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            border: 1px solid #ffeeba;\r\n            color: #856404;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .tip-box {\r\n            background-color: #d4edda;\r\n            border: 1px solid #c3e6cb;\r\n            color: #155724;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        ul {\r\n            padding-left: 20px;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        li {\r\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .correct-answer {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #27ae60;\r\n            font-size: 18px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            margin: 20px 0;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            border: 2px dashed #27ae60;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n\r\n    <!-- 标题卡片 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析：管制性征收<br><span class=\"english-term\" style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: normal;\">Regulatory Takings</span></h1>\r\n        <p>本题考察的是美国宪法第五修正案（Fifth Amendment）中的<b>征收条款（Takings Clause）</b>，特别是当政府法规导致财产价值完全丧失时的法律后果。</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 正确答案 -->\r\n    <div class=\"correct-answer\">\r\n        正确答案：D\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 核心解析 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>深度解析</h2>\r\n        <p>法院很可能会判决购买者胜诉，理由如下：</p>\r\n        \r\n        <p><b>1. 管制性征收 (Regulatory Taking)</b><br>\r\n        虽然政府没有物理上占有土地，但如果一项法规剥夺了所有者对该财产<b>“所有经济上有利的用途”</b> (<span class=\"english-term\">all economically beneficial use</span>)，这在法律上被视为一种“本身即构成征收” (<span class=\"english-term\">per se taking</span>)。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>2. 事实认定</b><br>\r\n        题目中明确指出：\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>法规禁止了<b>所有</b>建设 (<span class=\"english-term\">prohibited all construction</span>)。</li>\r\n            <li>该财产现在<b>一文不值</b> (<span class=\"english-term\">worthless</span>)。</li>\r\n            <li>购买者无法出售或租赁该土地。</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n        这种程度的限制完全剥夺了购买者<b>“有投资支持的预期”</b> (<span class=\"english-term\">investment-backed expectations</span>)，即开发房产的计划。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>3. 结论</b><br>\r\n        根据第五修正案，当法规效果等同于完全剥夺财产价值时，政府必须支付<b>公正补偿</b> (<span class=\"english-term\">Just Compensation</span>)，无论政府的初衷（如环境保护）多么高尚。</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 判例指引 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>关键判例 (Key Precedent)</h2>\r\n        <div class=\"case-box\">\r\n            <strong>Lucas v. South Carolina Coastal Council (1992)</strong><br><br>\r\n            最高法院在该案中确立了规则：当一项法规剥夺了土地所有者<b>100%</b>的经济价值时，除非该限制源于普通法中的妨害（nuisance）原则，否则政府必须进行赔偿。这就是著名的<b>“卢卡斯规则” (Lucas Rule)</b>。\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 干扰项排除 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>为什么其他选项是错的？</h2>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li><b>选项 A 错误：</b>征收不需要政府获得<b>所有权</b> (<span class=\"english-term\">title</span>)。只要政府行为剥夺了财产的使用权或价值，即可构成征收。</li>\r\n            <li><b>选项 B 错误：</b>这混淆了<b>物理性征收</b> (<span class=\"english-term\">Physical Taking</span>) 和管制性征收。虽然没有物理入侵，但法规限制本身已构成征收。</li>\r\n            <li><b>选项 C 错误：</b>这是一个常见的陷阱。虽然保护环境是合法的<b>警察权</b> (<span class=\"english-term\">Police Power</span>) 行使，但这并不能免除政府在造成“完全经济价值丧失”时的赔偿责任。目的正当不代表可以免费剥夺私产。</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 备考锦囊 -->\r\n    \r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
      "meta": {
