    {
      "index": 9,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Regulation Of Content",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "The Federal Family Film Enhancement Act assesses an excise tax of 10% on the price of admission to public movie theaters when they show films that contain actual or simulated scenes of human sexual intercourse.\nWhich of the following is the strongest argument against the constitutionality of this federal act?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "The act imposes a prior restraint on the freedom of speech protected by the First Amendment.",
        "B": "The act imposes a tax solely on the basis of the content of speech without adequate justification and, therefore, it is prohibited by the freedom of speech clause of the First Amendment.",
        "C": "The act is not rationally related to any legitimate national interest.",
        "D": "The act violates the equal protection concepts embodied in the due process clause of the Fifth Amendment because it imposes a tax on the price of admission to view certain films and not on the price of admission to view comparable live performances."
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0009.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\" />\n<title>Explanation</title>\n<style>\n  body{\n    margin:0;\n    font-size:1rem;\n    line-height:1.7;\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    color:#111;\n    background:#fff;\n  }\n  .pbx-explanation{\n    padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;\n    box-sizing:border-box;\n    max-width:100%;\n  }\n  .pbx-explanation, .pbx-explanation *{\n    box-sizing:border-box;\n  }\n  .pbx-wrap{\n    max-width:100%;\n  }\n  .pbx-table-title{\n    text-align:center;\n    font-weight:700;\n    font-size:1.35rem;\n    padding:0.65em 0;\n    border:1px solid #000;\n    border-bottom:none;\n  }\n  .pbx-scroll-x{\n    overflow-x:auto;\n    -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;\n    margin:16px 0;\n  }\n  table{\n    min-width:480px;\n    width:100%;\n    border-collapse:collapse;\n    border:1px solid #cccccc;\n  }\n  th, td{\n    border:1px solid #cccccc;\n    padding:8px 12px;\n    vertical-align:top;\n    font-size:1rem;\n  }\n  th{\n    background:#f5f5f5;\n    font-weight:bold;\n  }\n  .pbx-center{\n    text-align:center;\n  }\n  .pbx-edu-objective{\n    background:#f0f7ff;\n    border-left:4px solid #3498db;\n    border-radius:6px;\n    padding:14px 18px;\n    margin:24px 0;\n  }\n  .pbx-edu-objective-title{\n    font-size:13px;\n    font-weight:700;\n    color:#2980b9;\n    text-transform:uppercase;\n    letter-spacing:0.05em;\n    margin-bottom:8px;\n  }\n  .pbx-references{\n    background:#fafafa;\n    border:1px solid #e0e0e0;\n    border-radius:6px;\n    padding:14px 18px;\n    margin:20px 0;\n  }\n  .pbx-references-title{\n    font-size:13px;\n    font-weight:700;\n    color:#555;\n    text-transform:uppercase;\n    letter-spacing:0.05em;\n    margin-bottom:8px;\n  }\n  .pbx-ref-list{\n    margin:0;\n    padding-left:18px;\n    font-size:14px;\n    color:#555;\n    line-height:1.7;\n  }\n  .pbx-choice{\n    margin:0 0 1em 0;\n  }\n  .pbx-choice[data-choice-role=\"correct\"]{\n    border-left:3px solid #27ae60;\n    padding-left:10px;\n  }\n  .pbx-choice[data-choice-role=\"distractor\"]{\n    border-left:3px solid #c0392b;\n    padding-left:10px;\n  }\n  .pbx-correct{ color:#1f8f4d; font-weight:600; }\n  .pbx-wrong{ color:#9b1c1c; font-weight:600; }\n  .pbx-mixed{ color:#b07d00; font-weight:600; }\n  p{ margin:0 0 1em 0; }\n  ul{ margin:0 0 1em 1.25em; }\n  li{ margin:0.2em 0; }\n  .pbx-strong{ font-weight:700; }\n  @media (max-width:640px){\n    body{ font-size:0.95rem; padding:0.75rem; }\n    .pbx-explanation{ padding:0.875rem 1rem; }\n    th, td{ font-size:0.825rem; padding:0.5em 0.625em; }\n    .pbx-table-title{ font-size:1.15rem; }\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Regulation Of Content -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <div class=\"pbx-wrap\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-table-title\">Speech regulations</div>\n    <div class=\"pbx-scroll-x\">\n      <table>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th class=\"pbx-center\">Type</th>\n            <th class=\"pbx-center\">Definition</th>\n            <th class=\"pbx-center\">Test</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Content-based</strong></td>\n            <td>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Facial discrimination</li>\n                <li>Primary purpose targets message, subject, or idea</li>\n              </ul>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n              <div>Strict scrutiny</div>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Necessary &amp; narrowly tailored to achieve compelling interest</li>\n              </ul>\n            </td>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <td><strong>Content-neutral</strong></td>\n            <td>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Regulates time, place, or manner of speech</li>\n              </ul>\n            </td>\n            <td>\n              <div>Intermediate scrutiny</div>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Narrowly tailored to achieve important interest</li>\n                <li>Alternative avenues of communication remain</li>\n              </ul>\n            </td>\n          </tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>The First Amendment <strong>free speech clause</strong> protects the right to freely communicate and receive information and ideas. To ensure such protection, <strong>content-based restrictions</strong> on speech are <strong>presumptively unconstitutional</strong> and subject to <strong>strict scrutiny</strong>. This means that the government can only restrict speech based on what is being said (ie, its message or ideas) if it can prove that the restriction is <strong>necessary and narrowly tailored</strong> to achieve a <strong>compelling government interest</strong>—a nearly impossible task.</p>\n\n    <p>Here, the act is a content-based restriction on speech because it imposes an excise tax on the price of admission to theaters when they show films that depict human sexual intercourse. And since it is highly unlikely that this act can survive strict scrutiny, the strongest argument against its constitutionality is that it imposes a tax based solely on the content of speech without adequate justification.</p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice A)</strong> A prior restraint on speech is a highly disfavored government action that prohibits speech before it even occurs (eg, injunction). But the act here is not a prior restraint on speech because it does not prevent the films from being shown—it merely imposes a tax.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"correct\"><strong style=\"color:#1f8f4d\">(Choice B)</strong> The act imposes a tax solely on the basis of the content of speech without adequate justification and, therefore, it is prohibited by the freedom of speech clause of the First Amendment.</div>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"C\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice C)</strong> If the federal act is <em>not</em> rationally related to a legitimate national interest, it cannot pass rational basis scrutiny—<em>let alone</em> strict scrutiny. But this argument would likely fail since laws almost always survive rational basis review.</p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"D\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice D)</strong> This act may trigger the equal protection concepts embodied in the Fifth Amendment, which apply when the government treats similarly situated people differently. But since the movie theater patrons who must pay this tax are not part of a protected class, this is not a strong argument for challenging the act's validity.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n      <p>Content-based restrictions on speech are unconstitutional unless they survive strict scrutiny. This incredibly stringent standard requires the government to prove that the restriction is necessary and narrowly tailored to achieve a compelling government interest.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n      <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n        <li>Ark. Writers' Project, Inc. v. Ragland, 481 U.S. 221, 231 (1987) (applying strict scrutiny to a tax scheme that exempts certain magazines based on content).</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "下列哪项是反对该联邦法案合宪性的最有力论点？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "该法案对受《第一修正案》保护的言论自由施加了事先限制。",
        "B": "该法案仅基于言论内容征税，且无充分正当理由，因此，该行为被《第一修正案》的言论自由条款所禁止。",
        "C": "该法案与任何合法的国家利益均不存在理性关联。",
        "D": "该法案违反了《第五修正案》正当程序条款所体现的平等保护理念，因为它对观看某些电影的门票价格征税，而对观看可比的现场表演的门票价格则不征税。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #e74c3c;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #ecf0f1;\r\n            --text-color: #34495e;\r\n            --border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f4f4;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            background: #ffffff;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n        .header {\r\n            background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .header h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 1.2em;\r\n            font-weight: 700;\r\n        }\r\n        .header .sub-title {\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-box {\r\n            background-color: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            border-left: 5px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n            display: block;\r\n        }\r\n.term {\n            background: transparent;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(36, 52, 71, 0.26);\n            padding: 0 1px 1px;\n            border-radius: 0;\n            font-size: 1em;\n            font-weight: 800;\n            white-space: normal;\n        }\r\n        .english-term {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n        }\r\n        .analysis-section {\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .analysis-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            font-size: 1.1em;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            padding-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .option-analysis {\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n        }\r\n        .correct-tag {\r\n            background-color: #27ae60;\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 2px 6px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n            font-size: 0.8em;\r\n            margin-right: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong-tag {\r\n            background-color: #95a5a6;\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 2px 6px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n            font-size: 0.8em;\r\n            margin-right: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .case-ref {\r\n            font-size: 0.85em;\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            margin-top: 10px;\r\n            border-top: 1px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-top: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n        .strategy-tip {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            border: 1px solid #ffeeba;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            font-size: 0.95em;\r\n        }\r\n        .strategy-header {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #856404;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <div class=\"sub-title\">宪法第一修正案与税收</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 核心考点 -->\r\n        <div class=\"rule-box\">\r\n            <span class=\"rule-title\">核心原则：基于内容的规制 (Content-Based Regulation)</span>\r\n            当政府对言论施加限制（包括税收）是基于言论的<b>内容</b>（即所表达的信息、主题或思想）时，该行为被推定为违宪，必须接受<span class=\"term\">严格审查</span> <span class=\"english-term\">(Strict Scrutiny)</span>。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 正确答案解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"analysis-section\">\r\n            <div class=\"analysis-title\">为何选项 B 是正确答案？</div>\r\n            <p>本题的核心在于识别该税收的性质。这项联邦税并非适用于所有电影票的通用销售税，而是<b>专门针对</b>包含特定内容（性交场景）的电影。</p>\r\n            \r\n            <p><b>1. 识别歧视：</b><br>\r\n            最高法院在 <i>Arkansas Writers' Project, Inc. v. Ragland</i> 等判例中确立，针对特定出版物或言论内容的差别税收（Differential Taxation）属于基于内容的规制。</p>\r\n\r\n            <p><b>2. 适用标准：</b><br>\r\n            因为是基于内容的，政府必须证明该法律满足<span class=\"term\">严格审查</span>标准：\r\n            <ul>\r\n                <li>必须为了实现<b>迫切的政府利益</b> <span class=\"english-term\">(Compelling Government Interest)</span>。</li>\r\n                <li>手段必须是<b>狭义限定</b>的 <span class=\"english-term\">(Narrowly Tailored)</span>。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n            </p>\r\n\r\n            <p><b>3. 结论：</b><br>\r\n            仅仅为了增加收入通常不足以构成“迫切利益”来正当化对言论内容的歧视。因此，最有力的论点是该法案基于内容征税且缺乏充分（迫切）的正当理由。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 干扰项解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"analysis-section\">\r\n            <div class=\"analysis-title\">其他选项为何不够强？</div>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"option-analysis\">\r\n                <span class=\"wrong-tag\">选项 A</span> <b>事先限制 (Prior Restraint)</b><br>\r\n                虽然事先限制也是违宪的，但税收通常被视为事后的负担，而不是阻止言论发表的“禁令”或“许可制度”。除非税额高到构成事实上的禁止，否则法院更倾向于将其视为基于内容的惩罚，而非事先限制。\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"option-analysis\">\r\n                <span class=\"wrong-tag\">选项 C</span> <b>理性基础 (Rational Basis)</b><br>\r\n                这是一个陷阱。涉及言论自由的限制需要更高标准的审查（严格审查或中度审查），而不仅仅是“理性关联”。如果只用理性基础测试，政府很容易通过（例如声称为了保护家庭价值观），但这在第一修正案下是不够的。\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"option-analysis\">\r\n                <span class=\"wrong-tag\">选项 D</span> <b>平等保护 (Equal Protection)</b><br>\r\n                虽然差别待遇涉及平等保护，但在涉及基本权利（如言论自由）时，法院通常直接依据第一修正案进行分析。第一修正案的分析比第五修正案的平等保护分析更直接、更具体地针对言论内容歧视问题。\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        <div class=\"strategy-tip\">\r\n            <div class=\"strategy-header\">💡 MBE 考试技巧</div>\r\n            <p>看到政府对媒体、电影或出版物征税时，请立即检查：</p>\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li><b>通用税 (General Tax)：</b>如果是对所有企业一视同仁的税，通常合宪。</li>\r\n                <li><b>特定税 (Specific Tax)：</b>如果是专门针对媒体，或者针对特定<b>内容</b>的媒体征税，这就触发了<b>严格审查</b>。</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n            <p>本题中，“仅针对有性交场景的电影”就是明显的“基于内容”的信号。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"case-ref\">\r\n            <b>Reference Case:</b> <i>Arkansas Writers' Project, Inc. v. Ragland</i>, 481 U.S. 221 (1987).\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
