    {
      "index": 13,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Free exercise",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A police officer was employed on a city's police force for 10 years. When the officer accepted the job, the city's employee benefit plan provided a death benefit to the spouse of any employee who died as a result of any job-related injury. Last year, the city amended its employee benefit plan to deny its death benefit in cases where the death \"was caused by the employee's refusal to accept, for any reason, reasonably available medical care prescribed by a physician.\"\nAfter this amendment took effect, the officer was shot while on duty. Because of a sincerely held religious belief, the officer refused to allow a prescribed blood transfusion and, as a result, died from loss of blood. When the officer's spouse applied for the death benefit, the city denied the application on the basis of the amendment to the employee benefit plan.\nThe officer's spouse has challenged the amendment, claiming that, as applied to the officer, it violated the officer's constitutional right to the free exercise of religion.\nIs the court likely to find the amendment to the employee benefit plan constitutional as applied to the officer?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because it effectively discriminates against a religious practice.",
        "B": "No, because it violates the vested contractual rights of city employees who were hired before the amendment took effect.",
        "C": "Yes, because it is generally applicable and religiously neutral, as well as a reasonable limitation on the award of such benefits.",
        "D": "Yes, because it imposes a condition only on the award of a government benefit and does not impose a penalty on an individual's conduct."
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0013.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n      background: #fff;\n      color: #111;\n      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation {\n      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      max-width: 100%;\n      word-break: break-word;\n      overflow-wrap: break-word;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation p {\n      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-wrap {\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-inner {\n      min-width: 34rem;\n      max-width: 100%;\n      width: 100%;\n      display: flex;\n      flex-direction: column;\n      align-items: center;\n      color: #222;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-title {\n      font-size: 1.25rem;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-node {\n      background: #f7f9fc;\n      border-radius: 0.75rem;\n      box-shadow: 0 0.2rem 0.45rem rgba(0,0,0,0.18);\n      border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;\n      text-align: center;\n      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-root {\n      width: 19rem;\n      font-size: 1.08rem;\n      line-height: 1.25;\n      margin-bottom: 1.55rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-branch-line {\n      width: 22rem;\n      height: 1.4rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      border-top: 2px solid #555;\n      border-right: 2px solid #555;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n      position: relative;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-branch-line:before,\n    .pbx-flow-branch-line:after {\n      content: \"\";\n      position: absolute;\n      top: -0.02rem;\n      width: 0;\n      height: 2.2rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-branch-line:before { left: 0; }\n    .pbx-flow-branch-line:after { right: 0; }\n    .pbx-flow-branches {\n      width: 100%;\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: space-between;\n      gap: 2rem;\n      margin-top: 1.2rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-col {\n      flex: 1 1 0;\n      display: flex;\n      flex-direction: column;\n      align-items: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-card {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 18rem;\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border-radius: 0.75rem;\n      box-shadow: 0 0.22rem 0.45rem rgba(0,0,0,0.18);\n      border: 1px solid #dfdfdf;\n      overflow: hidden;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-card-head {\n      background: #d9d9d9;\n      font-weight: 400;\n      padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;\n      font-size: 1.05rem;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-card-body {\n      padding: 0.8rem 1rem 0.9rem;\n      background: #f5f7fa;\n      text-align: left;\n      font-size: 0.98rem;\n      line-height: 1.35;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-card-body ul {\n      margin: 0.35rem 0 0 1.1rem;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-card-body li {\n      margin: 0.15rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-arrow {\n      width: 0;\n      height: 2.2rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      margin: 0.15rem 0;\n      position: relative;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-arrow:after {\n      content: \"\";\n      position: absolute;\n      left: -0.35rem;\n      bottom: -0.1rem;\n      width: 0.6rem;\n      height: 0.6rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      border-bottom: 2px solid #555;\n      transform: rotate(-45deg);\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-bottom {\n      width: 100%;\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: space-between;\n      gap: 2rem;\n      margin-top: 0.2rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-bottom p {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 18rem;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 1.06rem;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      line-height: 1.2;\n      margin: 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-choice {\n      border-left: 3px solid #c0392b;\n      padding-left: 10px;\n    }\n    .pbx-choice strong {\n      color: #9b1c1c;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding-left: 18px;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      color: #555;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-small-gap { margin-top: 1.5rem; }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation { padding: 0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-inner { min-width: 34rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-title { font-size: 1.1rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-root { font-size: 0.98rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-card-head { font-size: 0.95rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-card-body { font-size: 0.875rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-bottom p { font-size: 0.92rem; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- pbx-topic: Free exercise -->\n  <div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-flow-wrap\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-flow-inner\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-title\">Free exercise analysis</div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-node pbx-flow-root\">Government burdens<br>religious belief or conduct</div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-branch-line\"></div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-branches\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-col\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-flow-card\">\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-card-head\">Direct burden</div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-card-body\">\n                Strict scrutiny\n                <ul>\n                  <li>burden necessary to achieve</li>\n                  <li>compelling state interest</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"pbx-flow-arrow\"></div>\n            <p>Burden usually<br>unconstitutional</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-col\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-flow-card\">\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-card-head\">Incidental burden</div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-card-body\">\n                Rational basis\n                <ul>\n                  <li>burden rationally related to</li>\n                  <li>legitimate state interest</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"pbx-flow-arrow\"></div>\n            <p>Burden usually<br>constitutional</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>The First Amendment <strong>free exercise clause</strong> prohibits governments from denying benefits (or imposing burdens) based on an individual's religious belief or conduct <span data-choice=\"D\" data-choice-role=\"correct\" style=\"color:#1f8f4d;font-weight:600;\">(Choice D)</span>. The level of scrutiny applied to laws or policies that <strong>burden religion</strong> depends on whether that burden was:</p>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>direct</strong> (intentional) – triggering <strong>strict scrutiny</strong>, which invalidates a law unless the government proves that it is necessary to achieve a compelling government interest or</li>\n      <li><strong>incidental</strong> (generally applicable and religiously neutral) – triggering <strong>rational basis scrutiny</strong>, which upholds a law unless the challenger proves that the law has no rational relation to any legitimate government interest.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <p>But even an incidental burden will trigger <strong>strict scrutiny</strong> when the law requires an <strong>individualized assessment</strong> of a person's actions.</p>\n\n    <p>Here, the employee benefit plan only imposes an incidental burden since the plan is generally applicable to all employees and does not intentionally target religion (ie, is religiously neutral). That is because the plan denies benefits when the refusal to accept medical care was for any reason—it does not single out religious reasons (ie, no individualized assessment). And since the plan is reasonably related to the city's legitimate interest in limiting the award of benefits to job-related deaths, it is likely constitutional.</p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong>(Choice A)</strong> Although the benefit plan effectively discriminates against the officer's religious practice, the plan will likely be upheld since it is generally applicable and there is no evidence that it intentionally interfered with his religion.</p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong>(Choice B)</strong> The contracts clause prohibits state and municipal legislatures from enacting laws that substantially impair vested contract rights. But it does not apply to amendments to employee benefit plans since they are unrelated to lawmaking or rulemaking.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n      <p>Direct burdens on religion are strictly scrutinized and struck down unless the government proves that the law is necessary to achieve a compelling government interest. In contrast, incidental burdens are upheld unless the challenger proves that the law has no rational relation to any legitimate government interest.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n      <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n        <li>Emp't Div. v. Smith, 494 U.S. 872, 884–85 (1990) (affirming the government's ability to enforce a generally applicable law that incidentally burdens religion).</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一名警官在一个城市的警察部队中受雇了10年。当该警官接受这份工作时，该市的员工福利计划规定，任何因公受伤而死亡的员工的配偶将获得死亡抚恤金。去年，该市修改了其员工福利计划，规定在死亡“因员工出于任何原因拒绝接受医生开具的合理可行的医疗护理”而导致的情况下，拒绝发放死亡抚恤金。<br><br>在该修正案生效后，这名警官在执勤时中枪。由于真诚的宗教信仰，该警官拒绝接受医生开具的输血治疗，并因此失血过多而死亡。当该警官的配偶申请死亡抚恤金时，该市根据员工福利计划的修正案拒绝了其申请。<br><br>该警官的配偶对该修正案提出质疑，声称该修正案在适用于该警官时，侵犯了其自由行使宗教的宪法权利。<br><br>法院是否可能认定该员工福利计划修正案在适用于该警官时符合宪法？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不会，因为它实际上歧视了一种宗教实践。",
        "B": "不会，因为它侵犯了在该修正案生效前受雇的城市员工的既得合同权利。",
        "C": "会，因为它是普遍适用和宗教中立的，并且是对授予此类福利的合理限制。",
        "D": "会，因为它仅对授予政府福利设定了条件，并未对个人行为施加惩罚。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #e8f4f8;\r\n            --text-color: #333;\r\n            --border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        \r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            background-color: #f4f4f4;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            background: #fff;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header {\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary-color);\r\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header h2 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header span {\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .answer-box {\r\n            background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .answer-box h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 2.5rem;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .answer-box p {\r\n            margin: 5px 0 0 0;\r\n            font-size: 1rem;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .section-title {\r\n            color: var(--accent-color);\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: center;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .section-title::before {\r\n            content: '';\r\n            display: inline-block;\r\n            width: 4px;\r\n            height: 18px;\r\n            background-color: var(--accent-color);\r\n            margin-right: 8px;\r\n            border-radius: 2px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .concept-card {\r\n            background-color: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n            font-size: 0.95rem;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .key-term {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .english-term {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .trap-alert {\r\n            border: 1px solid #e74c3c;\r\n            background-color: #fdedec;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .trap-title {\r\n            color: #c0392b;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        ul {\r\n            padding-left: 20px;\r\n            margin: 10px 0;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        li {\r\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .footer {\r\n            margin-top: 30px;\r\n            font-size: 0.8rem;\r\n            color: #95a5a6;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            border-top: 1px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-top: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h2>宪法 (Constitutional Law)</h2>\r\n        <span>MBE 考点解析：自由行使条款</span>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n        <h1>C</h1>\r\n        <p>正确答案</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"section-title\">核心法律规则 (The Rule)</div>\r\n    <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n        <p>根据美国最高法院在 <span class=\"key-term\">Employment Division v. Smith (1990)</span> 一案中的裁决：</p>\r\n        <p>如果一项法律是<b>普遍适用的 (Generally Applicable)</b> 且 <b>宗教中立的 (Religiously Neutral)</b>，即使它附带地 (Incidentally) 限制了某种宗教行为，也不需要通过<b>严格审查 (Strict Scrutiny)</b>。</p>\r\n        <p>此类法律只需通过<b>合理基础审查 (Rational Basis Review)</b>，即只要法律与政府的合法利益有合理关联即可。</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"section-title\">本题解析 (Analysis)</div>\r\n    <p>要判断法院是否会支持该修正案，我们需要分析该法律的性质：</p>\r\n    <ul>\r\n        <li><b>中立性 (Neutrality)：</b> 该修正案规定拒绝福利的情况是员工“出于<b>任何原因</b> (for any reason)”拒绝医疗护理。它并没有专门针对宗教原因，也没有将世俗原因排除在外。</li>\r\n        <li><b>普遍适用性 (General Applicability)：</b> 该规定适用于所有城市员工，不针对特定群体。</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n    <p>因此，尽管该规定实际上导致了这位因宗教信仰拒绝输血的警官无法获得福利（附带负担），但因为法律本身是中立和普遍适用的，法院<b>不会</b>应用严格审查。</p>\r\n    <p><b>结论：</b> 政府为了节省开支或限制福利仅用于不可避免的死亡，具有<b>合法利益 (Legitimate Interest)</b>，而该修正案与此利益合理相关。因此，该修正案符合宪法。</p>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"trap-alert\">\r\n        <div class=\"trap-title\">⚠️ 高频陷阱：选项 B (合同条款)</div>\r\n        <p>很多考生会误选 <b>选项 B</b>，因为该市确实改变了员工入职时的福利条款，这看起来像是违反了<b>合同条款 (Contracts Clause)</b>。</p>\r\n        <p><b>为什么 B 是错的？</b></p>\r\n        <p>请仔细阅读题目的<b>提问 (Call of the Question)</b>：</p>\r\n        <p><i>\"...claiming that... it violated the officer's <b>constitutional right to the free exercise of religion</b>.\"</i></p>\r\n        <p>题目明确问的是基于<b>自由行使宗教权利</b>的挑战是否会成功，而不是基于合同权利的挑战。虽然基于合同条款的挑战可能会成功，但这与本题的诉讼请求（宗教自由）无关。</p>\r\n        <p><b>MBE 技巧：</b> 永远针对题目中特定的法律主张进行回答，不要因为发现了一个潜在的（但未被提出的）违法点而偏离主题。</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"section-title\">其他选项排除</div>\r\n    <ul>\r\n        <li><b>选项 A：</b> 错误。虽然法律产生了歧视性的<b>效果</b>，但只要没有歧视性的<b>目的</b>（即法律是中立的），就不会违反自由行使条款。</li>\r\n        <li><b>选项 D：</b> 错误。这涉及“违宪条件原则” (Unconstitutional Conditions)，通常用于政府不能强迫个人放弃权利以换取福利。但在 <i>Smith</i> 案原则下，只要条件是中立通用的，政府通常可以设定福利资格标准。选项 C 的理由更直接切中 <i>Smith</i> 案的要害。</li>\r\n    </ul>\r\n\r\n    \r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
      "meta": {
