    {
      "index": 14,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Free exercise",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A generally applicable state statute requires an autopsy by the county coroner in all cases of death that are not obviously of natural causes. The purpose of this law is to ensure the discovery and prosecution of all illegal activity resulting in death. In the 50 years since its enactment, the statute has been consistently enforced.\nA married couple are sincere practicing members of a religion that maintains it is essential for a deceased person's body to be buried promptly and without any invasive procedures, including an autopsy. When the couple's son died of mysterious causes and an autopsy was scheduled, they filed an action in state court challenging the constitutionality of the state statute and seeking an injunction prohibiting the county coroner from performing an autopsy on their son's body. In this action, the couple claimed only that applying this statute in the circumstances of their son's death would violate their right to the free exercise of religion as guaranteed by the First and Fourteenth Amendments. Assume that no federal statutes are applicable.\nIs the state's autopsy statute constitutional as applied to the couple?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because it is not necessary to vindicate a compelling state interest.",
        "B": "No, because it is not substantially related to an important state interest.",
        "C": "Yes, because a dead individual is not a person protected by the due process clause of the Fourteenth Amendment.",
        "D": "Yes, because it is a generally applicable statute and is rationally related to a legitimate state purpose."
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0014.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body{\n      margin:0;\n      font-size:1rem;\n      line-height:1.7;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      color:#111;\n      background:#fff;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation{\n      padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing:border-box;\n      max-width:100%;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation *{\n      box-sizing:border-box;\n    }\n    .pbx-center{\n      text-align:center;\n    }\n    .pbx-title{\n      font-size:1.35rem;\n      font-weight:700;\n      text-align:center;\n      margin:0 0 1.2rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-wrap{\n      margin:0.5rem auto 1.2rem auto;\n    }\n    .pbx-scroll-x{\n      overflow-x:auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;\n      margin:16px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-inner{\n      min-width:720px;\n      padding:0.25rem 0.5rem 0.75rem 0.5rem;\n      margin:0 auto;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-top{\n      width:22rem;\n      margin:0 auto;\n      border:1px solid #d6d6d6;\n      border-radius:0.85rem;\n      background:#f4f7fb;\n      text-align:center;\n      padding:0.95rem 1rem;\n      box-shadow:0 0.2rem 0.35rem rgba(0,0,0,0.22);\n      font-size:1rem;\n      line-height:1.35;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-line{\n      width:0.15rem;\n      height:2.2rem;\n      background:#666;\n      margin:0 auto;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-branch{\n      display:flex;\n      justify-content:center;\n      align-items:flex-start;\n      gap:2.2rem;\n      position:relative;\n      margin-top:0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-branch:before{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      top:0;\n      left:50%;\n      transform:translateX(-50%);\n      width:24rem;\n      height:0.15rem;\n      background:#666;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-col{\n      width:22rem;\n      padding-top:1.2rem;\n      position:relative;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-col:before{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      top:0;\n      left:50%;\n      width:0.15rem;\n      height:1.2rem;\n      background:#666;\n      transform:translateX(-50%);\n    }\n    .pbx-card{\n      border:1px solid #d2d2d2;\n      border-radius:0.9rem;\n      overflow:hidden;\n      box-shadow:0 0.14rem 0.25rem rgba(0,0,0,0.12);\n      background:#fff;\n    }\n    .pbx-card-h{\n      background:#dedede;\n      padding:0.6rem 0.9rem;\n      font-size:1rem;\n      text-align:center;\n      font-weight:400;\n    }\n    .pbx-card-b{\n      background:#f6f9fc;\n      padding:0.8rem 1rem 0.9rem 1rem;\n      font-size:0.98rem;\n      line-height:1.35;\n    }\n    .pbx-card-b ul{\n      margin:0.3rem 0 0 1.2rem;\n      padding:0;\n    }\n    .pbx-card-b li{\n      margin:0.15rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-footer{\n      display:flex;\n      justify-content:space-between;\n      gap:2rem;\n      margin-top:1.0rem;\n      font-size:1.02rem;\n      font-weight:700;\n      text-align:center;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-footer .pbx-foot-col{\n      width:22rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-down{\n      text-align:center;\n      font-size:1.6rem;\n      line-height:1;\n      margin:0.2rem 0;\n      color:#333;\n    }\n    p{\n      margin:0 0 1.05rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-indent{\n      margin-left:1.2rem;\n    }\n    ul{\n      margin:0.5rem 0 1rem 1.45rem;\n    }\n    li{\n      margin:0.2rem 0 0.45rem 0;\n    }\n    strong{ font-weight:700; }\n    em{ font-style:italic; }\n    .pbx-choice{\n      margin:0.7rem 0 0.95rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-choice strong{\n      font-weight:700;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective{\n      background:#f0f7ff;\n      border-left:4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius:6px;\n      padding:14px 18px;\n      margin:24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title{\n      font-size:13px;\n      font-weight:700;\n      color:#2980b9;\n      text-transform:uppercase;\n      letter-spacing:0.05em;\n      margin-bottom:8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references{\n      background:#fafafa;\n      border:1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius:6px;\n      padding:14px 18px;\n      margin:20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title{\n      font-size:13px;\n      font-weight:700;\n      color:#555;\n      text-transform:uppercase;\n      letter-spacing:0.05em;\n      margin-bottom:8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list{\n      margin:0;\n      padding-left:18px;\n      font-size:14px;\n      color:#555;\n      line-height:1.7;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 640px){\n      body{\n        font-size:0.95rem;\n        padding:0.75rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-explanation{\n        padding:0.875rem 1rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-title{\n        font-size:1.2rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-flow-inner{\n        min-width:640px;\n      }\n      .pbx-flow-top,.pbx-flow-col,.pbx-flow-footer .pbx-foot-col{\n        width:19rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-card-h,.pbx-card-b{\n        font-size:0.92rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-flow-footer{\n        font-size:0.95rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-references-title,.pbx-edu-objective-title{\n        font-size:12px;\n      }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- pbx-topic: Free exercise -->\n  <div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-title\">Free exercise analysis</div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-flow-wrap\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-scroll-x\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-inner\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-top\">Government burdens<br/>religious belief or conduct</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-line\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-branch\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-flow-col\">\n              <div class=\"pbx-card\">\n                <div class=\"pbx-card-h\">Direct burden</div>\n                <div class=\"pbx-card-b\">\n                  <div>Strict scrutiny</div>\n                  <ul>\n                    <li>burden necessary to achieve</li>\n                    <li>compelling state interest</li>\n                  </ul>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"pbx-flow-col\">\n              <div class=\"pbx-card\">\n                <div class=\"pbx-card-h\">Incidental burden</div>\n                <div class=\"pbx-card-b\">\n                  <div>Rational basis</div>\n                  <ul>\n                    <li>burden rationally related to</li>\n                    <li>legitimate state interest</li>\n                  </ul>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-footer\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-foot-col\">Burden usually<br/>unconstitutional</div>\n            <div class=\"pbx-foot-col\">Burden usually<br/>constitutional</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>The First Amendment, applicable to the states through the Fourteenth Amendment due process clause, protects an individual's <strong>right to freely exercise</strong> his/her <strong>sincerely held religious beliefs.</strong> Any government infringement on this right must satisfy the appropriate level of scrutiny, which depends on the <strong>type of burden</strong> imposed:</p>\n\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>direct</strong> (intentionally targets religion) – the burden is presumptively invalid and the state must prove that the burden is necessary to achieve a compelling state interest (ie, <strong>strict scrutiny</strong>)</li>\n      <li><strong>incidental</strong> (generally applies to all) – the burden is presumptively valid and the challenger must prove that the burden is not rationally related to any legitimate state interest (ie, <strong>rational basis scrutiny</strong>)</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <p>Here, the couple's sincere religious belief that bodies must be buried promptly and without any invasive procedures was burdened when the county coroner scheduled an autopsy of their son's body. But since a generally applicable state statute requires autopsies for <em>all</em> mysterious deaths like his, that burden is merely incidental. And since autopsies for suspicious deaths are rationally related to a legitimate state purpose—discovering and prosecuting illegal activity resulting in death—the statute is constitutional as applied to the couple.</p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice A)</strong> Had the state intentionally targeted the couple's religion, the state would have needed to prove that the statute was necessary to vindicate a compelling state interest (ie, strict scrutiny).</p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice B)</strong> Under the Fourteenth Amendment equal protection clause, laws that impact a quasi-suspect class must be substantially related to an important state interest (ie, intermediate scrutiny). But religion is not a quasi-suspect class, so this standard does not apply.</p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"C\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice C)</strong> A dead individual is not protected by the Fourteenth Amendment due process clause. But the couple's challenge of the statute is based on their own constitutional rights—not those of their dead son.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n      <p>The First Amendment protects the right to freely exercise one's sincerely held religious beliefs. Direct burdens (which target religion) are almost always unconstitutional under strict scrutiny. But incidental burdens (which apply to all) are usually constitutional under rational basis scrutiny.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n      <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n        <li>Emp't Div. v. Smith, 494 U.S. 872, 885 (1990) (holding that a generally applicable regulation on conduct need not satisfy strict scrutiny to comply with the First Amendment free exercise clause).</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一项普遍适用的州法规要求，在所有非明显自然原因导致的死亡案件中，县验尸官必须进行尸检。该法律的宗旨是确保发现并起诉所有导致死亡的非法活动。自该法规颁布以来的50年里，它一直得到持续执行。\n\n一对夫妇是某一宗教的虔诚教徒，该宗教坚称，逝者的遗体必须迅速下葬，且不得经过任何侵入性程序，包括尸检。当这对夫妇的儿子因不明原因死亡，且官方已安排进行尸检时，他们在州法院提起诉讼，质疑该州法规的合宪性，并寻求获得一项禁令，以禁止县验尸官对其子的遗体进行尸检。在该诉讼中，这对夫妇仅主张，在其子死亡的情况下适用该法规，将侵犯他们受 First and Fourteenth Amendments 保障的自由行使宗教信仰的权利。假定没有适用的联邦法规。\n\n该州的尸检法规适用于这对夫妇时是否合宪？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不合宪，因为它并非为维护一项紧迫的州利益所必需。",
        "B": "不合宪，因为它与一项重要的州利益没有实质性关联。",
        "C": "合宪，因为逝者并非受 Fourteenth Amendment 正当程序条款保护的“人”。",
        "D": "合宪，因为它是一项普遍适用的法规，且与一项合法的州目的具有理性关联。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f6f8;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            color: #333;\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            margin: 0 auto;\r\n            background: #ffffff;\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n        .header {\r\n            background-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .header h2 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 18px;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-box {\r\n            background-color: #e8f5e9;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid #4caf50;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-label {\r\n            color: #2e7d32;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n            text-transform: uppercase;\r\n            display: block;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-card {\r\n            background-color: #e3f2fd;\r\n            border: 1px solid #bbdefb;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-title {\r\n            color: #1565c0;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-title::before {\r\n            content: \"⚖️\";\r\n            margin-right: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        .section-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #34495e;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .case-ref {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #555;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong-option {\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            background-color: #fff5f5;\r\n            border-left: 3px solid #ef5350;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n            font-size: 0.95em;\r\n        }\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            padding: 0 4px;\r\n            border-radius: 2px;\r\n        }\r\n        .footer {\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            font-size: 12px;\r\n            color: #999;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h2>MBE 考点解析：自由行使条款</h2>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 正确答案部分 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n            <span class=\"answer-label\">正确答案：D</span>\r\n            <strong>合宪，因为它是一项普遍适用的法规，且与一项合法的州目的具有理性关联。</strong>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 核心法律规则 -->\r\n        <div class=\"rule-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"rule-title\">核心考点：Smith 规则</div>\r\n            <p>根据美国最高法院在 <span class=\"case-ref\">Employment Division v. Smith (1990)</span> 一案中的裁决：</p>\r\n            <p>如果一项法律是<b>中立的</b>（Neutral）且<b>普遍适用的</b>（Generally Applicable），即使它<b>附带地</b>（Incidentally）加重了宗教行为的负担，也不违反第一修正案的<b>自由行使条款</b>（Free Exercise Clause）。</p>\r\n            <p>此类法律只需通过<b>合理依据审查</b>（Rational Basis Review）。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 深度解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">📝 法律推理分析</div>\r\n        <p>本题考察的是当“普遍适用的州法律”与“个人宗教信仰”发生冲突时的审查标准。</p>\r\n        \r\n        <ol>\r\n            <li>\r\n                <strong>法律性质判断：</strong><br>\r\n                题目明确指出该尸检法规是“普遍适用的”（generally applicable），且目的是为了发现非法活动，并非针对特定宗教（not targeting religion）。\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li>\r\n                <strong>审查标准选择：</strong><br>\r\n                在 <i>Smith</i> 案之后，对于非针对宗教的普遍性法律，不再适用<b>严格审查</b>（Strict Scrutiny）。只要法律不是为了压制宗教，政府就不需要证明有“紧迫的州利益”（Compelling State Interest）。\r\n            </li>\r\n            <li>\r\n                <strong>应用合理依据审查：</strong><br>\r\n                法律只需与“合法的州目的”（Legitimate State Purpose）有“理性关联”（Rationally Related）。\r\n                <br>👉 <strong>本案中：</strong> 调查死因、起诉犯罪是合法的州目的，尸检是实现该目的的理性手段。因此，法律合宪。\r\n            </li>\r\n        </ol>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 错误选项辨析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">❌ 为什么其他选项错误？</div>\r\n        \r\n        <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n            <strong>选项 A (Strict Scrutiny)：</strong>\r\n            错误。严格审查仅在法律<b>专门针对</b>宗教，或涉及联邦法律（受 RFRA 限制）时才适用。本题是州法律且普遍适用。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n            <strong>选项 B (Intermediate Scrutiny)：</strong>\r\n            错误。中度审查（实质性关联 + 重要利益）通常用于性别歧视或商业言论等，不适用于自由行使宗教条款的分析。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n            <strong>选项 C (Due Process/Standing)：</strong>\r\n            错误。虽然死者没有正当程序权利，但本案的原告是<b>父母</b>，他们主张的是<b>自己</b>的宗教自由权利（处理亲属遗体），这足以构成诉讼资格（Standing）。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        <div class=\"rule-card\" style=\"background-color: #fff8e1; border-color: #ffe082;\">\r\n            <div class=\"rule-title\" style=\"color: #f57f17;\">💡 MBE 考试技巧</div>\r\n            <p>看到 <b>Free Exercise Clause</b>（自由行使条款）的题目时，首先判断：</p>\r\n            <ul style=\"margin-bottom:0; padding-left: 20px;\">\r\n                <li>是<b>针对宗教</b>的法律？ ➡️ 选 Strict Scrutiny（通常违宪）。</li>\r\n                <li>是<b>普遍适用</b>的中立法律？ ➡️ 选 Rational Basis（通常合宪）。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n            <p style=\"font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 8px;\"><b>注意陷阱：</b>如果题目提到 RFRA（宗教自由恢复法案），则联邦行为必须满足严格审查。但本题明确说“无联邦法规适用”。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    \r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
      "meta": {
        "question_analysis": {
          "micro_concept": "Free exercise incidental burden analysis",
          "trap_type": "Rule Exception Overlooked",
          "trap_type_is_new": false,
          "skill_tested": "Apply constitutional free exercise scrutiny",
          "question_keyword_meta": {
            "keywords": [
              {
                "id": "k1",
                "text": "generally applicable state statute",
                "label": "English / 普遍適用的州法",
                "kind": "legal_term",
                "reason": "判斷自由行使條款的審查標準關鍵",
                "importance": "high"
