    {
      "index": 16,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Significant state involvement",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "Insurance is provided in a state only by private companies. Although the state insurance commissioner inspects insurance companies for solvency, the state does not regulate their rates or policies. An insurance company charges higher rates for burglary insurance to residents of one part of a county in the state than to residents of another section of the same county because of the different crime rates in those areas.\nA resident of that county was charged the higher rate by the insurance company because of the location of her residence. She sues the insurance company, alleging that the differential in insurance rates unconstitutionally denies her the equal protection of the laws.\nWill the resident's suit succeed?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because the constitutional guarantee of equal protection of the laws is not applicable to the actions of these insurance companies.",
        "B": "No, because there is a rational basis for the differential in insurance rates.",
        "C": "Yes, because the higher crime rate in the resident's neighborhood demonstrates that the county police are not giving persons who reside there the equal protection of the laws.",
        "D": "Yes, because the insurance rate differential is inherently discriminatory."
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0016.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; background: #fff; color: #111; }\n    .pbx-explanation { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; box-sizing: border-box; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; }\n    .pbx-explanation p { margin: 0 0 1rem 0; word-break: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; }\n    .pbx-explanation strong { font-weight: 700; }\n    .pbx-explanation em { font-style: italic; }\n    .pbx-explanation u { text-decoration: underline; }\n    .pbx-explanation .pbx-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; margin: 1rem 0; }\n    .pbx-explanation table { min-width: 480px; width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 1px solid #cccccc; }\n    .pbx-explanation th, .pbx-explanation td { border: 1px solid #cccccc; padding: 0.5em 0.625em; vertical-align: top; }\n    .pbx-explanation th { background: #f5f5f5; font-weight: bold; }\n    .pbx-explanation ul { margin: 0 0 1rem 1.5rem; padding: 0; }\n    .pbx-explanation li { margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0; }\n    .pbx-center { text-align: center; }\n    .pbx-title { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 700; }\n    .pbx-edu-objective { background: #f0f7ff; border-left: 4px solid #3498db; border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px 18px; margin: 24px 0; }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #2980b9; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n    .pbx-references { background: #fafafa; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px 18px; margin: 20px 0; }\n    .pbx-references-title { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #555; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n    .pbx-ref-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 14px; color: #555; line-height: 1.7; }\n    .pbx-flow-inner { min-width: 720px; }\n    .pbx-small-gap { margin-top: 0.4rem; }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation { padding: 0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-title { font-size: 1.1rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation th, .pbx-explanation td { font-size: 0.825rem; padding: 0.5em 0.625em; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Significant state involvement -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <div class=\"pbx-table-wrap\">\n    <table>\n      <tr>\n        <th colspan=\"2\" class=\"pbx-center\"><span class=\"pbx-title\">State-action doctrine</span></th>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th style=\"width:31%;\">Traditional government<br>function</th>\n        <td>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Private actor performs traditional &amp; exclusive government function<br>(eg, running elections)</li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th>Significant government<br>involvement</th>\n        <td>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Government &amp; private actor have <em>mutually beneficial</em> relationship (eg, joint activity or venture)</li>\n            <li>Government creates <em>nexus</em> by affirmatively facilitating or authorizing private action (eg, police officer acting under color of law)</li>\n            <li>Government is <em>pervasively intertwined</em> in private entity's management or control</li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>The Constitution (excluding the Thirteenth Amendment) only applies to government actors. But in rare circumstances, <strong>a private actor is viewed as a government actor</strong> (and subject to the Constitution) under the <strong>state-action doctrine</strong>. This doctrine applies when:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li>the private actor performs a <strong>traditional and exclusive government function</strong> or</li>\n    <li>the government is <strong>significantly involved</strong> in the private actor's activities.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>Therefore, the resident can only challenge the private insurance company's <strong>discriminatory conduct</strong> on <u>equal protection</u> grounds if the state-action doctrine applies.</p>\n\n  <p>Here, the company does not perform a traditional and exclusive government function since insurance has historically been provided by private entities. And though the state inspects all insurance companies for solvency, it does not regulate their rates and policies. But even if it did, state regulation (however substantial) does not amount to <em>significant government involvement</em> since this is an <em>ordinary</em> government activity. Therefore, the resident's suit will fail because equal protection guarantees do not apply to the company's actions.</p>\n\n  <p data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice B)</strong> Equal protection challenges undergo rational basis review when the challenged action does not impact a fundamental right or <u>protected class</u>. But since the insurance company's actions cannot be challenged on equal protection grounds, it does not matter whether there is a rational basis for the insurance rate differential.</p>\n\n  <p><strong>(Choices C &amp; D)</strong> The higher crime rate in the resident's neighborhood may demonstrate that county police are not giving neighborhood residents the equal protection of the laws. And the insurance rate differential is inherently discriminatory. But these facts are irrelevant in this suit against a <em>private</em> insurance company.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n    <p>The state-action doctrine applies when (1) a private actor performs a traditional and exclusive government function or (2) the government is significantly involved in the private actor's activities. The private actor is then treated as a government actor and bound by the Constitution.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n    <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n      <li>Am. Mfrs. Mut. Ins. Co. v. Sullivan, 526 U.S. 40, 52 (1999) (holding that private insurance companies are not government actors unless there is proof of significant government involvement in their activities).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "某州的保险业务仅由私营公司提供。尽管州保险专员会对保险公司的偿付能力进行检查，但州政府并不监管其费率或保单。一家保险公司对该州某县部分地区的居民收取的入室犯法罪保险费率高于同一县另一地区的居民，原因是这些地区的犯罪率不同。\n\n该县的一名居民因其住所位置而被该保险公司收取了较高的费率。她起诉该保险公司，声称保险费率的差异违宪地剥夺了她受法律平等保护的权利。\n\n该居民的诉讼会成功吗？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不会，因为宪法关于法律平等保护的保障不适用于这些保险公司的行为。",
        "B": "不会，因为保险费率的差异存在理性基础。",
        "C": "会，因为该居民社区较高的犯罪率表明，县警察未能给予居住在此的居民法律的平等保护。",
        "D": "会，因为保险费率的差异本质上是歧视性的。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #e8f4f8;\r\n            --text-color: #333;\r\n            --card-bg: #ffffff;\r\n            --border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f4f4;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            width: 100%;\r\n            background: var(--card-bg);\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header {\r\n            background: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header .sub-title {\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .answer-box {\r\n            background: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            border-left: 5px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .answer-label {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            display: block;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .concept-card {\r\n            border: 1px solid #eee;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .concept-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--accent-color);\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-bottom: 8px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            font-size: 16px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            padding: 2px 4px;\r\n            border-radius: 2px;\r\n            font-weight: 500;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .english-term {\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .logic-step {\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: flex-start;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .step-icon {\r\n            background: var(--accent-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            width: 24px;\r\n            height: 24px;\r\n            border-radius: 50%;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: center;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n            margin-right: 10px;\r\n            flex-shrink: 0;\r\n            font-size: 12px;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .wrong-option {\r\n            margin-top: 15px;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n            color: #666;\r\n            border-top: 1px dashed #ddd;\r\n            padding-top: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .exam-tip {\r\n            background-color: #27ae60;\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .exam-tip strong {\r\n            display: block;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n            font-size: 16px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考题解析</h1>\r\n        <div class=\"sub-title\">宪法 (Constitutional Law) - 个人权利</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 正确答案 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n            <span class=\"answer-label\">正确答案：选项 A</span>\r\n            <p>不会，因为宪法关于法律平等保护的保障不适用于这些保险公司的行为。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 核心考点 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\">核心考点：州行为理论 (State Action Doctrine)</div>\r\n            <p>美国宪法第十四修正案的<strong>平等保护条款 (Equal Protection Clause)</strong> 仅限制政府（州）的行为，而不限制私人行为。</p>\r\n            <p>除非存在例外情况，否则私人公司（如本题中的保险公司）的歧视性行为不构成违宪。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 逻辑推演 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\">解题逻辑推演</div>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n                <div class=\"step-icon\">1</div>\r\n                <div>\r\n                    <strong>识别主体：</strong><br>\r\n                    题目明确指出保险是由“私营公司” (private companies) 提供的。\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n                <div class=\"step-icon\">2</div>\r\n                <div>\r\n                    <strong>判断是否构成“州行为”：</strong><br>\r\n                    私营主体要被视为政府行为者，必须满足以下极其严格的条件之一：\r\n                    <ul>\r\n                        <li><strong>公共职能 (Public Function)：</strong> 该实体履行了传统上由政府独占的职能（如选举）。保险显然不是。</li>\r\n                        <li><strong>纠缠/关联 (Entanglement/Nexus)：</strong> 政府必须积极授权、鼓励或促进该违宪行为。</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n                <div class=\"step-icon\">3</div>\r\n                <div>\r\n                    <strong>分析政府监管：</strong><br>\r\n                    题目中提到州政府“检查偿付能力” (inspects for solvency) 但“不监管费率” (does not regulate rates)。<br>\r\n                    <span class=\"highlight\">单纯的政府监管或发放牌照并不足以将私人行为转化为州行为。</span>\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n                <div class=\"step-icon\">4</div>\r\n                <div>\r\n                    <strong>结论：</strong><br>\r\n                    由于没有“州行为”，宪法不适用。无论费率差异多么不公平，原告无法依据宪法起诉。\r\n                </div>\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 错误选项分析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n            <strong>为什么其他选项是错的？</strong>\r\n            <ul style=\"padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;\">\r\n                <li><strong>选项 B (Rational Basis)：</strong> 只有确定宪法适用后，才进行审查标准（如理性基础审查）的分析。既然宪法不适用，审查标准就无从谈起。</li>\r\n                <li><strong>选项 C & D：</strong> 这些选项讨论了事实上的不公平或歧视性。虽然这些可能是事实，但在缺乏“州行为”的前提下，它们不能作为<strong>宪法诉讼</strong>的依据。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        <div class=\"exam-tip\">\r\n            <strong>💡 MBE 考试技巧</strong>\r\n            <p>当你在宪法题中看到被告是<strong>私人个体或公司</strong>时，第一反应必须是检查是否存在<strong>州行为 (State Action)</strong>。</p>\r\n            <p>如果政府仅仅是颁发执照、提供水电服务或进行一般性监管，通常<strong>不构成</strong>州行为。如果不存在州行为，直接选择“宪法不适用”类的选项。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
