    {
      "index": 20,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Establishment",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A city ordinance created a three-member zoning board, which is responsible for approving the location of all entertainment venues in the city. In an inseverable provision, the ordinance requires that one member of the board be a representative of the local council of churches.\nA minister was appointed to the board to represent the local council of churches. During the minister's tenure, the board denied a company permission to open a nightclub in a particular location solely because it would be so close to an existing church that it might disturb the church's operations. The company has challenged the ordinance and its application in federal court on constitutional grounds.\nIs the company likely to prevail?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because the existing church has a right to have its vested property interests protected.",
        "B": "No, because the minister was only one of three votes and, therefore, could not dictate the decision of the zoning board.",
        "C": "Yes, because, as applied, the ordinance denied the company the equal protection of the laws by irrationally discriminating against its particular type of business.",
        "D": "Yes, because the requirement that the zoning board include a representative of the local council of churches violates the First and Fourteenth Amendments."
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0020.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body{margin:0;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background:#fff;color:#111}\n    .pbx-explanation{padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;box-sizing:border-box;max-width:100%}\n    .pbx-explanation *{box-sizing:border-box}\n    .pbx-wrap{max-width:980px;margin:0 auto}\n    .pbx-figure{width:100%;margin:0 0 1rem 0}\n    .pbx-figure img{display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:4px;box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.18)}\n    .pbx-title{font-size:2.1rem;line-height:1.15;font-weight:700;text-align:center;margin:1.1rem 0 1rem}\n    .pbx-body{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7}\n    .pbx-body p{margin:0 0 1rem}\n    .pbx-body strong{font-weight:700}\n    .pbx-edu-objective{background:#f0f7ff;border-left:4px solid #3498db;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 18px;margin:24px 0}\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2980b9;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;margin-bottom:8px}\n    .pbx-references{background:#fafafa;border:1px solid #e0e0e0;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 18px;margin:20px 0}\n    .pbx-references-title{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#555;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;margin-bottom:8px}\n    .pbx-ref-list{margin:0;padding-left:18px;font-size:14px;color:#555;line-height:1.7}\n    .pbx-ref-list li{margin:0 0 .5rem}\n    .pbx-choice{border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px}\n    .pbx-choice-correct{border-left-color:#27ae60}\n    .pbx-choice-label-wrong{color:#9b1c1c;font-weight:600}\n    .pbx-choice-label-correct{color:#1f8f4d;font-weight:600}\n    .pbx-linklike{color:#2b6cb0;text-decoration:underline}\n    @media (max-width:640px){\n      body{font-size:.95rem;padding:.75rem}\n      .pbx-explanation{padding:.875rem 1rem}\n      .pbx-title{font-size:1.7rem}\n      .pbx-body{font-size:.95rem}\n      .pbx-ref-list{font-size:14px}\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Establishment -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <div class=\"pbx-wrap\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-figure\">\n      <img alt=\"Wall separating church and state\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" />\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-body\">\n      <p>A law that <strong>benefits or burdens religion</strong> can be challenged under the First Amendment <strong>establishment clause</strong>, as applied to states and municipalities through the Fourteenth Amendment. This clause places a <strong>wall of separation between church and state</strong>. But this wall contains gates that can be opened if the government passes the appropriate test. The busiest gate—the <strong>historical test</strong>—opens when a law has <strong>historically been permitted in accordance with the original meaning of the Constitution.</strong></p>\n\n      <p>Here, an ordinance requires that one member of the zoning board be a representative of the local council of churches. However, guaranteeing religious institutions positions on government boards and committees has historically not been permitted under the original meaning of the Constitution. Since the ordinance requires membership by a church representative on the zoning board, the gates of the establishment-clause wall should remain closed. Therefore, the company will likely prevail.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice A)</strong> Although the church has a vested interest in its property, this interest can only be protected by constitutional means—eg, religiously neutral zoning decisions.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"pbx-choice pbx-choice-correct\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice B)</strong> The minister had only one of three votes and could not dictate the zoning board's decision. But the provision granting him a spot on the board is still unconstitutional as violative of the establishment clause.</p>\n\n      <p class=\"pbx-choice\" data-choice=\"C\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice C)</strong> The <span class=\"pbx-linklike\">equal protection clause</span> can be used to invalidate a law that is applied in a discriminatory manner. But since there is no evidence that similarly situated businesses were permitted to open near a church, there is no proof of discrimination against the company. As a result, it is unlikely to prevail on this basis.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n        <p>The historical test allows the government to pass through the First Amendment establishment-clause wall separating church and state when the government action has historically been permitted in accordance with the original meaning of the Constitution.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n        <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n          <li>Larkin v. Grendel's Den, 459 U.S. 116, 125–27 (1982) (holding that a law that delegates or shares important government powers with a religious institution violates the First Amendment establishment clause).</li>\n          <li>Kennedy v. Bremerton School Dist., 142 S. Ct. 2407, 2428 (2022) (holding that challenges based on the establishment clause \"must be interpreted by reference to historical practices and understandings\").</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一项城市法令设立了一个由三名成员组成的分区委员会，该委员会负责批准市内所有娱乐场所的选址。该法令中一项不可分割的条款要求，委员会的一名成员必须是当地教会理事会的代表。\n\n一名牧师被任命为委员会成员，以代表当地教会理事会。在该牧师的任期内，委员会拒绝了一家公司在特定地点开设夜总会的许可，唯一的原因是该地点离一个现有教堂太近，可能会干扰教堂的运作。该公司已在联邦法院以宪法为由，对该法令及其实施提出质疑。\n\n该公司有可能胜诉吗？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不会，因为现有教堂有权使其既得财产利益受到保护。",
        "B": "不会，因为该牧师仅有三票中的一票，因此无法决定分区委员会的决策。",
        "C": "会，因为该法令在实施中，通过非理性地歧视该公司的特定业务类型，剥夺了该公司受法律平等保护的权利。",
        "D": "会，因为要求分区委员会包含一名当地教会理事会代表的规定，违反了第一修正案和第十四修正案 (First and Fourteenth Amendments)。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    <title>MBE 考点解析</title>\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f4f9;\r\n            color: #333;\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            background: #fff;\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n        .header {\r\n            background-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .header h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n        .header .sub-title {\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-box {\r\n            background-color: #e8f5e9;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid #4caf50;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-label {\r\n            color: #2e7d32;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n            text-transform: uppercase;\r\n        }\r\n        .section-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #2c3e50;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            padding: 2px 4px;\r\n            border-radius: 3px;\r\n            font-weight: 500;\r\n        }\r\n        .case-study {\r\n            background-color: #e3f2fd;\r\n            border: 1px solid #bbdefb;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin: 15px 0;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n        .case-title {\r\n            color: #1565c0;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n            display: block;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong-choice {\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\r\n            border-bottom: 1px dashed #eee;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong-choice:last-child {\r\n            border-bottom: none;\r\n        }\r\n        .badge {\r\n            display: inline-block;\r\n            padding: 2px 8px;\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            font-size: 12px;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-right: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .badge-wrong {\r\n            background-color: #ffebee;\r\n            color: #c62828;\r\n        }\r\n        .exam-tip {\r\n            background-color: #fff8e1;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid #ffc107;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-top: 25px;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n        .latin {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #555;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <div class=\"sub-title\">宪法权利 · 政教分离条款</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 正确答案部分 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n            <div class=\"answer-label\">正确答案：D</div>\r\n            <p>是的，因为要求分区委员会包含一名当地教会理事会代表的规定，违反了第一修正案和第十四修正案。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 核心考点解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">⚖️ 法律依据与推理</div>\r\n        \r\n        <p>本题的核心考点是<b>第一修正案的政教分离条款 (Establishment Clause)</b>。该条款禁止政府制定任何关于确立宗教的法律。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>1. 政府权力的委托 (Delegation of Power)：</b><br>\r\n        最高法院在 <i>Larkin v. Grendel's Den</i> (1982) 一案中确立了原则：政府不能将重要的政府权力（如分区审批权）直接委托给宗教机构。在本题中，法令强制要求分区委员会 (Zoning Board) 的一名成员必须是“教会理事会代表”。这实际上是将政府的决策权与宗教机构融合了。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>2. 历史测试 (Historical Test)：</b><br>\r\n        根据最新的最高法院判例（如 <i>Kennedy v. Bremerton School Dist.</i>），判断是否违反政教分离条款主要看<b>历史实践和理解 (Historical Practices and Understandings)</b>。在美国宪法历史上，并没有允许宗教机构在政府决策委员会中拥有“保留席位”的传统。这种做法打破了教会与国家之间的隔离。</p>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"case-study\">\r\n            <span class=\"case-title\">🔍 关键判例关联</span>\r\n            在 <i>Larkin</i> 案中，马萨诸塞州的一项法律赋予教堂否决其附近酒牌申请的权力。最高法院裁定该法违宪，因为它将传统的政府职能（分区/许可）通过法律形式交给了宗教团体。本题中的法令虽然是给予“席位”而非直接否决权，但逻辑相同：它赋予了宗教机构行使世俗政府权力的特权。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 错误选项解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">❌ 为什么其他选项错误？</div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-choice\">\r\n            <span class=\"badge badge-wrong\">选项 A</span>\r\n            <b>既得财产利益 (Vested Property Interests)：</b><br>\r\n            虽然教会有权保护其财产，但这不能成为政府违反宪法第一修正案的理由。政府保护财产利益必须通过<b>宗教中立 (Religiously Neutral)</b> 的方式，而不是通过赋予教会政府席位。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-choice\">\r\n            <span class=\"badge badge-wrong\">选项 B</span>\r\n            <b>仅有一票 (One Vote)：</b><br>\r\n            这是一个常见的干扰项。违宪的关键在于<b>委员会的构成 (Composition)</b> 本身是非法的。法令强制要求宗教代表入驻政府机构，这本身就违反了政教分离原则。无论该牧师是否拥有决定性的一票，这种权力的融合 (Entanglement) 已经发生。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-choice\">\r\n            <span class=\"badge badge-wrong\">选项 C</span>\r\n            <b>平等保护 (Equal Protection)：</b><br>\r\n            虽然平等保护条款禁止非理性的歧视，但在本案中，分区决策通常基于土地使用类型（如夜总会 vs 教堂）。如果政府有合理的理由（如噪音控制），区分对待不同业务通常能通过理性基础审查 (Rational Basis Review)。相比之下，<b>政教分离条款</b>的违宪是显而易见且致命的。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        \r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
