    {
      "index": 23,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Establishment",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "Several public high school students asked the superintendent of their public school district whether the minister of a local church could deliver an interdenominational prayer at their graduation ceremony in the school auditorium. None of the students or their guests at graduation would be required to pray while the minister delivered the prayer.\nWould the minister's delivery of such a prayer at the public high school graduation be constitutional?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because it would be an unconstitutional establishment of religion.",
        "B": "No, because it would deny attendees who are not members of the minister's denomination the right to freely exercise their religion.",
        "C": "Yes, because none of the students or their guests would be required to pray at the graduation ceremony.",
        "D": "Yes, because the idea for the prayer originated with the students and not with school officials."
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0023.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      color: #111;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation {\n      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      max-width: 100%;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      color: #111;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation p {\n      margin: 0 0 1em 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-title {\n      text-align: center;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      font-size: 1.375rem;\n      margin: 0.25em 0 0.75em;\n    }\n    .pbx-scroll-x {\n      overflow-x: auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;\n      margin: 1em 0;\n    }\n    table {\n      min-width: 480px;\n      width: 100%;\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n      table-layout: fixed;\n      background: #fff;\n    }\n    th, td {\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n      padding: 8px 12px;\n      vertical-align: top;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.65;\n      word-break: break-word;\n      overflow-wrap: break-word;\n    }\n    th {\n      background: #f5f5f5;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding-left: 18px;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      color: #555;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-note {\n      font-size: 0.95rem;\n      font-style: italic;\n    }\n    .pbx-footer-spacer {\n      height: 0.5rem;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation { padding: 0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-title { font-size: 1.2rem; }\n      th, td { font-size: 0.825rem; padding: 0.5em 0.625em; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Establishment -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <table>\n    <tr>\n      <th colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size:1.25rem;\">Establishment clause tests</th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th style=\"width:18%;\">Test</th>\n      <th style=\"width:40%;\">Requirements</th>\n      <th style=\"width:42%;\">Applicability</th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td><strong>Historical*</strong></td>\n      <td>• Longstanding tradition &amp; historical foundation</td>\n      <td>Default</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td><strong>Endorsement</strong></td>\n      <td>• No appearance that government endorses religion</td>\n      <td>Public displays or monuments (eg, holiday displays)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td><strong>Coercion</strong></td>\n      <td>• No forced conformity with religious belief or practice</td>\n      <td>Public schools (eg, convocation prayer)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size:0.95rem;\">*Courts may apply strict scrutiny if government directly benefits/burdens religion.</td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n\n  <p>The <strong>First Amendment establishment clause</strong> prohibits the government from expressing a religious preference or otherwise violating the <strong>separation of church and state</strong>. In <em>Lee v. Weisman</em>, the Supreme Court held that <strong>school-sponsored prayer</strong> must be reviewed under the <strong>coercion test</strong>, which considers whether the government <strong>forced participation in a religious exercise</strong>. Under this test, prayer that occurs <em>during school events</em> (such as graduation) is generally seen as involuntary, and thus unconstitutional.</p>\n\n  <p>Since elementary and secondary school students are more susceptible to social and peer pressure than adults, school-sponsored prayer in these public schools is inherently coercive—even when participation is voluntary <span data-choice=\"C\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"color:#9b1c1c;font-weight:600;\">(Choice C)</span>. As a result, the minister's delivery of a prayer during the public high school graduation would be an unconstitutional establishment of religion.*</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-note\">*This result is not impacted by the Supreme Court's decision in <em>Kennedy v. Bremerton School District</em>. That case involved a football coach engaging in and leading voluntary prayer that was not sponsored by the school and occurred <u>after</u> a football game. As a result, there was no coercion of students or players to participate.</p>\n\n  <p data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice B)</strong> Since participation would be voluntary, the minister's prayer would not deny attendees the right to freely exercise their own religion. But the prayer would still violate the <span style=\"color:#1f8f4d;text-decoration: underline;\">establishment clause</span>—despite being interdenominational—because it would show government preference for religion in general.</p>\n\n  <p data-choice=\"D\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice D)</strong> Although the graduation prayer was the students' idea, the school still must abide by the Constitution if it approves that idea and sponsors the prayer.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n    <p>Under the coercion test, school-sponsored prayer in public schools violates the establishment clause even when participation is voluntary.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n    <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n      <li>Lee v. Weisman, 505 U.S. 577, 592–93 (1992) (holding that an interdenominational prayer at middle school graduation ceremony coerces religious participation in violation of the establishment clause).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "几名公立高中的学生询问其学区负责人，一名当地教堂的牧师是否可以在学校礼堂举行的毕业典礼上进行跨教派的祈祷。在牧师祈祷时，毕业典礼上的学生或其宾客均不被要求一同祈祷。\n\n在公立高中的毕业典礼上，由牧师进行这样的祈祷是否合宪？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不合宪，因为这将构成违宪的国教确立。",
        "B": "不合宪，因为这将剥夺那些非该牧师所属教派成员的与会者自由信奉其宗教的权利。",
        "C": "合宪，因为毕业典礼上的学生或其宾客均不被要求进行祈祷。",
        "D": "合宪，因为祈祷的想法源于学生，而非学校官员。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n\r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n    :root {\r\n        --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n        --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n        --correct-color: #27ae60;\r\n        --wrong-color: #c0392b;\r\n        --bg-color: #f4f6f7;\r\n        --card-bg: #ffffff;\r\n    }\r\n    body {\r\n        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n        background-color: var(--bg-color);\r\n        margin: 0;\r\n        padding: 10px;\r\n        color: #333;\r\n        line-height: 1.6;\r\n    }\r\n    .container {\r\n        max-width: 480px;\r\n        margin: 0 auto;\r\n        background-color: var(--card-bg);\r\n        border-radius: 12px;\r\n        box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n        overflow: hidden;\r\n    }\r\n    .header {\r\n        background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n        color: white;\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n        text-align: center;\r\n    }\r\n    .header h1 {\r\n        margin: 0;\r\n        font-size: 20px;\r\n        font-weight: 700;\r\n    }\r\n    .header p {\r\n        margin: 5px 0 0;\r\n        font-size: 14px;\r\n        opacity: 0.9;\r\n    }\r\n    .content {\r\n        padding: 20px;\r\n    }\r\n    .answer-box {\r\n        background-color: #e8f8f5;\r\n        border-left: 5px solid var(--correct-color);\r\n        padding: 15px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        border-radius: 4px;\r\n    }\r\n    .answer-title {\r\n        color: var(--correct-color);\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n        font-size: 18px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n    }\r\n    .section-title {\r\n        font-size: 16px;\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n        color: var(--primary-color);\r\n        margin-top: 20px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n        border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;\r\n        padding-bottom: 5px;\r\n    }\r\n    .concept-card {\r\n        background-color: #f8f9fa;\r\n        border: 1px solid #e9ecef;\r\n        border-radius: 8px;\r\n        padding: 15px;\r\n        margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n    }\r\n    .case-law {\r\n        background-color: #fff8e1;\r\n        border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;\r\n        padding: 10px 15px;\r\n        font-size: 14px;\r\n        margin: 10px 0;\r\n        font-style: italic;\r\n    }\r\n    .key-term {\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n        color: var(--accent-color);\r\n    }\r\n    .wrong-option {\r\n        margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n        font-size: 14px;\r\n    }\r\n    .wrong-option span {\r\n        color: var(--wrong-color);\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n    }\r\n    .exam-tip {\r\n        background-color: #e3f2fd;\r\n        padding: 15px;\r\n        border-radius: 8px;\r\n        margin-top: 20px;\r\n        font-size: 14px;\r\n    }\r\n    .exam-tip-title {\r\n        color: var(--accent-color);\r\n        font-weight: bold;\r\n        margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        display: flex;\r\n        align-items: center;\r\n    }\r\n    .icon {\r\n        margin-right: 5px;\r\n    }\r\n</style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <p>宪法：个人权利 / 国教条款</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 正确答案部分 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n            <div class=\"answer-title\">✅ 正确答案：A</div>\r\n            <p>不合宪，因为这将构成违宪的国教确立 (Unconstitutional Establishment of Religion)。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 核心考点解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">⚖️ 法律依据：胁迫测试 (Coercion Test)</div>\r\n        <p>本题的核心考点在于宪法第一修正案的<b>国教条款 (Establishment Clause)</b> 在公立学校环境中的适用。</p>\r\n        \r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <p>最高法院在处理公立学校祈祷问题时，主要适用<b>胁迫测试 (Coercion Test)</b>。该测试认为，政府不得强迫任何人支持或参与宗教活动。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"case-law\">\r\n            <span class=\"icon\">📜</span> <b>关键判例：Lee v. Weisman (1992)</b><br>\r\n            最高法院裁定，在公立学校毕业典礼上邀请神职人员进行祈祷是违宪的。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>推理逻辑如下：</b></p>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li><b>环境的特殊性：</b>中小学生比成年人更容易受到同伴压力 (Peer Pressure) 和社会压力。</li>\r\n            <li><b>心理胁迫 (Psychological Coercion)：</b>虽然学校声称“不要求一同祈祷”，但在毕业典礼这种重要场合，学生为了出席典礼，实际上被迫处于一种必须表现出尊重的宗教氛围中。</li>\r\n            <li><b>实质上的强制：</b>对于持不同信仰或无信仰的学生来说，如果不愿参与，他们唯一的选择就是缺席毕业典礼，这构成了实质上的强制参与。</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 错误选项解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">❌ 为什么其他选项是错的？</div>\r\n        \r\n        <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n            <span>选项 B 错误：</span>虽然祈祷可能让非信徒感到不适，但宪法禁止它的主要理由是政府<b>确立 (Establishment)</b> 了宗教，而不仅仅是阻碍了自由行使 (Free Exercise)。此外，自愿参与并未解决政府偏袒宗教的问题。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n            <span>选项 C 错误：</span>“自愿参与” (Voluntary) 在公立学校语境下是一个陷阱。根据 <i>Lee v. Weisman</i>，在学校组织的官方活动中，所谓的“自愿”往往带有内在的强制性。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"wrong-option\">\r\n            <span>选项 D 错误：</span>即使想法源于学生，但只要学校官员（如学区负责人）<b>批准、组织或发起</b>了该活动，这就变成了“政府行为” (State Action)，必须受到宪法约束。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        \r\n            <p>在处理 <b>Establishment Clause</b> 问题时，请注意区分场景：</p>\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li><b>公立学校 (Public Schools)：</b>审查最严格。通常适用<b>胁迫测试 (Coercion Test)</b>。凡是学校发起、组织或背书的祈祷（如毕业典礼、球赛广播），即使名义上自愿，通常也违宪。</li>\r\n                <li><b>立法机构/成人环境：</b>审查较宽松。通常适用<b>历史传统测试 (Historical/Tradition Test)</b>（如议会开场祈祷通常是合宪的）。</li>\r\n                <li><b>私人言论 vs. 政府言论：</b>如果学生在午餐时私下祈祷，受 <i>Free Exercise Clause</i> 保护；如果是学校邀请牧师上台，受 <i>Establishment Clause</i> 禁止。</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
