    {
      "index": 27,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "General Considerations",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A city passed an ordinance requiring individuals to obtain a license in order to care for children under the age of 12 for pay. City officials who promoted the ordinance said that the licensing process would ensure that child-care workers were adequately regulated for the health and safety of the city's children. To receive a license, the ordinance requires an individual to complete 10 hours of instruction in child care, undergo a background check, and pay a $100 fee. The ordinance affects women disproportionately to men, because female child-care workers far outnumber male child-care workers in the city.\nIs the ordinance constitutional?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because it has a disparate impact on women without a showing that the ordinance is necessary to serve a compelling government interest.",
        "B": "No, because it infringes on the freedom of contract without a compelling government interest.",
        "C": "Yes, because any burden it imposes is clearly outweighed by an important government objective.",
        "D": "Yes, because it is rationally related to a legitimate government objective."
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0027.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; background: #fff; color: #111; }\n    .pbx-explanation { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; box-sizing: border-box; max-width: 100%; }\n    .pbx-explanation * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    .pbx-explanation h1, .pbx-explanation h2, .pbx-explanation h3, .pbx-explanation p { margin: 0 0 1em 0; }\n    .pbx-explanation h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 700; text-align: center; margin: 0.25em 0 0.9em; }\n    .pbx-explanation h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.3; font-weight: 400; text-align: center; margin: 0; }\n    .pbx-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; align-items: start; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.2rem; }\n    .pbx-col h4 { font-size: 1.02rem; font-weight: 400; text-align: center; margin: 0 0 0.7rem; }\n    .pbx-card {\n      border: 1px solid #d9d1c5;\n      background: #fff;\n      min-height: 18rem;\n      padding: 0.75rem;\n      overflow: hidden;\n    }\n    .pbx-doc {\n      background: linear-gradient(180deg, #efe7d9 0%, #f6efe4 100%);\n      border: 1px solid #c9bea9;\n      padding: 0.85rem 0.75rem;\n      min-height: 18rem;\n      font-family: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n      color: #1a1a1a;\n    }\n    .pbx-doc .pbx-small { font-size: 0.72rem; }\n    .pbx-doc .pbx-title { font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 700; text-align: center; margin: 0.5rem 0; }\n    .pbx-panel {\n      background: #dfe7f1;\n      min-height: 18rem;\n      padding: 0.75rem;\n      position: relative;\n      overflow: hidden;\n    }\n    .pbx-badge {\n      display: inline-block;\n      padding: 0.12rem 0.55rem;\n      border-radius: 0.55rem;\n      background: #fff;\n      font-size: 0.9rem;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);\n    }\n    .pbx-speech {\n      display: inline-block;\n      background: #fff;\n      border-radius: 999px;\n      padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;\n      font-size: 0.9rem;\n      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.09);\n      max-width: 9rem;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-figure { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; margin-top: 1rem; gap: 0.75rem; }\n    .pbx-person { width: 31%; text-align: center; font-size: 0.78rem; }\n    .pbx-person .pbx-head { width: 2.7rem; height: 3.2rem; border-radius: 48% 48% 42% 42%; background: #c99; margin: 0 auto 0.2rem; }\n    .pbx-person .pbx-body { width: 100%; height: 5.2rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; background: #7f8fa6; }\n    .pbx-person:nth-child(2) .pbx-body { background: #5d8a57; }\n    .pbx-person:nth-child(3) .pbx-body { background: #d49a8d; }\n    .pbx-council {\n      background: #e5ded7;\n      min-height: 18rem;\n      padding: 0.75rem;\n      overflow: hidden;\n    }\n    .pbx-council .pbx-figure2 { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; align-items: center; margin-top: 1rem; }\n    .pbx-council .pbx-man { width: 35%; height: 11rem; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #8b5f4a, #c2a18c); border-radius: 0.7rem; }\n    .pbx-council .pbx-clerk { width: 28%; height: 12rem; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #e2e7ee, #8ea6bf); border-radius: 0.7rem; margin-left: auto; }\n    .pbx-council .pbx-paper { width: 32%; height: 5.2rem; background: #f7f2ea; border: 1px solid #b5aa9c; border-radius: 0.3rem; transform: rotate(-7deg); position: absolute; right: 1.6rem; bottom: 1.5rem; }\n    .pbx-text { font-size: 0.98rem; line-height: 1.65; }\n    .pbx-text strong { font-weight: 700; }\n    .pbx-list { margin: 0.35rem 0 1rem 1.4rem; padding: 0; }\n    .pbx-list li { margin: 0.28rem 0; }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 14px; color: #555; line-height: 1.7; }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation { padding: 0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n      .pbx-explanation h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation h3 { font-size: 1rem; }\n      .pbx-text { font-size: 0.93rem; }\n      .pbx-card, .pbx-doc, .pbx-panel, .pbx-council { min-height: 0; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: General Considerations -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <h2>Intentional discrimination</h2>\n  <div class=\"pbx-row\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-col\">\n      <h4>Facial discrimination</h4>\n      <div class=\"pbx-card pbx-doc\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-small\">S.789</div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-small\" style=\"text-align:center;margin-top:0.3rem;\">One Hundred Sixteenth Congress<br>of the<br>United States of America<br>AT THE FIRST SESSION</div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-title\">An Act</div>\n        <div style=\"font-size:1.05rem; line-height:1.5; margin-top:1rem;\">\n          <strong>Sec. Two</strong><br>\n          Males shall be<br>\n          preferred for<br>\n          government<br>\n          employment.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"pbx-col\">\n      <h4>Discriminatory application</h4>\n      <div class=\"pbx-card pbx-panel\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-badge\" style=\"display:block;text-align:center;margin:0 auto 0.4rem;width:max-content;\">STATE DMV</div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-badge\" style=\"display:block;text-align:center;margin:0 auto 0.8rem;font-weight:400;\">All applicants welcome!</div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-speech\" style=\"margin:0 auto 0.6rem; display:block;\">Only consider men.</div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-figure\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-person\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-head\"></div>\n            <div class=\"pbx-body\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-person\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-head\" style=\"background:#b7b7b7;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"pbx-body\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-person\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-head\" style=\"background:#d2b19f;\"></div>\n            <div class=\"pbx-body\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"pbx-col\">\n      <h4>Discriminatory impact</h4>\n      <div class=\"pbx-card pbx-council\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-badge\" style=\"display:block;text-align:center;margin:0 auto 0.4rem;width:max-content;\">CITY COUNCIL</div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-speech\" style=\"margin:0 auto 0.4rem; display:block; max-width: 10rem;\">This will keep most women out.</div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-figure2\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-man\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-clerk\"></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-paper\"></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-text\">\n    Discriminatory laws challenged under the <strong>equal protection clause</strong> are generally subject to rational basis scrutiny, which requires that a law be <strong>rationally related</strong> to a legitimate government objective. But heightened scrutiny is used when a law (1) substantially impacts a <span style=\"color:#1e73be;text-decoration:underline;\">fundamental right</span> or (2) intentionally discriminates against a suspect or quasi-suspect class. Intentional discrimination can be seen on a law's:\n    <ul class=\"pbx-list\">\n      <li><strong>face</strong> – the language of the law distinguishes between different classes (intent <em>presumed</em>)</li>\n      <li><strong>application</strong> – a facially neutral law is <em>purposefully</em> applied differently to different classes or</li>\n      <li><strong>motive</strong> – an otherwise neutral law was <em>enacted</em> to disproportionately impact a protected class.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    Here, although the ordinance disproportionately affects women (quasi-suspect class), it is not subject to heightened scrutiny since there is no evidence that this discrimination was <em>intentional</em>. That is because the ordinance:\n    <ul class=\"pbx-list\">\n      <li>requires that <strong>all</strong> child-care workers obtain a license (no facial discrimination)</li>\n      <li>is applied <strong>equally</strong> to men and women (no discriminatory application) and</li>\n      <li>was not enacted to target women (no discriminatory motive).</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    And since the ordinance is rationally related to the government's legitimate interest in the health and safety of children, it is constitutional.\n\n    <p data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice A)</strong> The city would have had to prove that the ordinance was necessary to serve a compelling government interest (ie, strict scrutiny) had it substantially impacted a fundamental right or intentionally discriminated against a suspect class. Since the ordinance does neither, it need only survive rational basis review.</p>\n\n    <p data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice B)</strong> The freedom of contract is protected by the contracts clause, which restricts state and local legislatures from impairing existing contracts. Since the ordinance affects the ability to enter into future contracts for child-care services, it does not violate this clause.</p>\n\n    <p data-choice=\"C\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice C)</strong> Had the ordinance intentionally discriminated against women, the city would have had to prove that the ordinance is substantially related to an important government objective (ie, intermediate scrutiny)– not that this objective clearly outweighs any burden the ordinance imposes.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n      <p>Heightened equal protection review is appropriate when a law intentionally discriminates—on its face, in its application, or in its motive—against a quasi-suspect or suspect class.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n      <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n        <li>U.S. Const. amend. XIV (equal protection clause).</li>\n        <li>Pers. Adm'r of Mass. v. Feeney, 442 U.S. 256, 274 (1979) (explaining that a neutral law's disparate impact on a quasi-suspect or suspect class, standing alone, is insufficient to require heightened scrutiny).</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "某市通过一项法令，要求为12岁以下儿童提供有偿看护服务的个人必须获得执照。推动该法令的市政官员表示，执照审批程序将确保托儿工作者受到充分监管，以保障本市儿童的健康与安全。根据该法令，要获得执照，个人必须完成10小时的托儿指导课程，接受背景调查，并支付100美元的费用。该法令对女性的影响不成比例地大于男性，因为在该市，女性托儿工作者的数量远超男性。\n\n该法令是否合宪？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不合宪，因为它对女性产生了不成比例的影响，且未能证明该法令对于服务于一项迫切的政府利益是必要的。",
        "B": "不合宪，因为它在没有迫切政府利益的情况下，侵犯了合同自由。",
        "C": "合宪，因为它所施加的任何负担显然被一项重要的政府目标所超越。",
        "D": "合宪，因为它与一项合法的政府目标具有理性关联。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #e8f4f8;\r\n            --text-color: #333;\r\n            --border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f4f4;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            background: #fff;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n        }\r\n        h1 {\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\r\n            margin-top: 0;\r\n        }\r\n        h2 {\r\n            font-size: 16px;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-box {\r\n            background-color: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding: 12px;\r\n            margin: 15px 0;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n        .key-term {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #e74c3c;\r\n        }\r\n        .english-term {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n        }\r\n        .logic-step {\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: flex-start;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n        .step-num {\r\n            background: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            width: 20px;\r\n            height: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 50%;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            line-height: 20px;\r\n            font-size: 12px;\r\n            margin-right: 10px;\r\n            flex-shrink: 0;\r\n        }\r\n        .option-analysis {\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n            border-top: 1px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-top: 10px;\r\n            margin-top: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n        .correct-tag {\r\n            color: #27ae60;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n        }\r\n        .wrong-tag {\r\n            color: #c0392b;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n        }\r\n        .tip-box {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            border: 1px solid #ffeeba;\r\n            padding: 12px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            font-size: 13px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <h1>MBE 考点解析：平等保护与差别影响</h1>\r\n    \r\n    <p>本题考查宪法第十四修正案<b>平等保护条款 (Equal Protection Clause)</b> 中的核心原则：如何审查表面中立但具有歧视性后果的法律。</p>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"rule-box\">\r\n        <strong>核心法则 (The Rule):</strong><br>\r\n        仅有<b>差别影响 (Disparate Impact)</b> 不足以触发严格审查或中度审查。必须证明存在<b>歧视意图 (Discriminatory Intent)</b>。<br><br>\r\n        如果法律表面中立且无歧视意图，即使它对某一受保护群体（如女性）产生不成比例的影响，也仅适用<b>理性基础审查 (Rational Basis Review)</b>。\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <h2>⚖️ 法律推理逻辑</h2>\r\n    \r\n    <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n        <div class=\"step-num\">1</div>\r\n        <div>\r\n            <strong>识别分类：</strong><br>\r\n            题目提到该法令对女性的影响大于男性。性别 (Gender) 通常属于“准可疑分类” (<span class=\"english-term\">Quasi-suspect classification</span>)，一般适用<b>中度审查 (Intermediate Scrutiny)</b>。\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n        <div class=\"step-num\">2</div>\r\n        <div>\r\n            <strong>检查歧视形式：</strong><br>\r\n            <ul>\r\n                <li><strong>表面歧视 (Facial Discrimination)？</strong> 无。法律文本写的是“个人 (individuals)”，未提及性别。</li>\r\n                <li><strong>歧视性适用 (Discriminatory Application)？</strong> 无。题目未提及只针对女性执法。</li>\r\n                <li><strong>歧视性动机 (Discriminatory Motive)？</strong> 无。题目明确指出目的是“儿童健康与安全”。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n        <div class=\"step-num\">3</div>\r\n        <div>\r\n            <strong>确定审查标准：</strong><br>\r\n            根据最高法院判例（如 <i>Washington v. Davis</i>），没有歧视意图的表面中立法律，仅需通过<b>理性基础审查</b>。\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"logic-step\">\r\n        <div class=\"step-num\">4</div>\r\n        <div>\r\n            <strong>应用标准：</strong><br>\r\n            政府目标（儿童安全）是合法的 (<span class=\"english-term\">Legitimate</span>)，手段（执照许可）与目标理性相关 (<span class=\"english-term\">Rationally related</span>)。因此合宪。\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <h2>🔍 选项深度解析</h2>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"option-analysis\">\r\n        <span class=\"correct-tag\">✅ 选项 D 正确</span><br>\r\n        它准确描述了理性基础审查的标准：“与合法的政府目标具有理性关联”。这是本案适用的正确标准，因为缺乏歧视意图。\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"option-analysis\">\r\n        <span class=\"wrong-tag\">❌ 选项 A 错误</span><br>\r\n        这是一个常见的干扰项。它错误地认为仅凭“差别影响”就需要政府证明“迫切利益” (<span class=\"english-term\">Compelling interest</span>，即严格审查)。实际上，如果没有歧视意图，不需要严格审查，甚至不需要中度审查。\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"option-analysis\">\r\n        <span class=\"wrong-tag\">❌ 选项 B 错误</span><br>\r\n        涉及<b>合同自由 (Freedom of Contract)</b>。自 <i>Lochner</i> 时代结束后，法院不再视合同自由为基本权利。经济和社会福利立法只需通过理性基础审查。此外，<b>合同条款 (Contracts Clause)</b> 仅禁止损害<i>现有</i>合同，不限制对<i>未来</i>商业行为的监管。\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"option-analysis\">\r\n        <span class=\"wrong-tag\">❌ 选项 C 错误</span><br>\r\n        该选项描述了一种类似“利益平衡”或中度审查的测试。虽然结果是“合宪”，但理由错误。本案不需要权衡负担是否被目标“超越”，只需证明手段与目的之间有理性关联即可。\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"tip-box\">\r\n        <strong>🎓 MBE 考试技巧 (Exam Tip):</strong><br>\r\n        看到“不成比例的影响” (<span class=\"english-term\">Disproportionate impact</span>) 时，立即寻找是否有<b>意图 (Intent)</b> 的证据。<br>\r\n        <ul>\r\n            <li>如果有意图 ➡️ 严格/中度审查。</li>\r\n            <li>如果只是意外后果（即使政府知道会有此后果）➡️ <b>理性基础审查 (Rational Basis)</b>。</li>\r\n        </ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
