    {
      "index": 31,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Miscellaneous",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A state statute provided state monetary grants to private dance, theater, and opera groups located in that state. The statute required recipients of such grants to use the granted monies for the acquisition, construction, and maintenance of appropriate facilities for the public performance of their performing arts. The last section of the statute conditioned the award of each such grant on the recipient's agreement to refrain from all kinds of political lobbying calculated to secure additional tax support for the performing arts.\nWhich of the following provides the strongest constitutional basis to attack the validity of the last section of the statute?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "Commerce clause.",
        "B": "Fifth Amendment.",
        "C": "First and Fourteenth Amendments.",
        "D": "Obligation of contracts clause."
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0031.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #111; background: #fff; }\n    .pbx-explanation { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; box-sizing: border-box; max-width: 100%; }\n    .pbx-explanation p { margin: 0 0 1rem 0; word-break: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word; }\n    .pbx-explanation strong { font-weight: 700; }\n    .pbx-explanation em { font-style: italic; }\n    .pbx-explanation .pbx-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; margin: 1rem 0; }\n    .pbx-explanation table { min-width: 480px; width: 100%; border: 1px solid #cccccc; border-collapse: collapse; }\n    .pbx-explanation th, .pbx-explanation td { border: 1px solid #cccccc; padding: 8px 12px; vertical-align: top; }\n    .pbx-explanation th { background: #f5f5f5; font-weight: bold; }\n    .pbx-explanation ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem; }\n    .pbx-explanation li { margin: 0.25rem 0; }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff; border-left: 4px solid #3498db; border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px; margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #2980b9; text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa; border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px; margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #555; text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 14px; color: #555; line-height: 1.7; }\n    .pbx-choice-correct { color: #1f8f4d; font-weight: 600; }\n    .pbx-choice-wrong { color: #9b1c1c; font-weight: 600; }\n    .pbx-choice-mixed { color: #b07d00; font-weight: 600; }\n    .pbx-choice-block-correct { border-left: 3px solid #27ae60; padding-left: 10px; }\n    .pbx-choice-block-wrong { border-left: 3px solid #c0392b; padding-left: 10px; }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation { padding: 0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation th, .pbx-explanation td { font-size: 0.825rem; padding: 0.5em 0.625em; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Miscellaneous -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-table-wrap\">\n    <table>\n      <tr>\n        <th colspan=\"3\">Conditions on government funding</th>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th style=\"width: 18%;\">Funded<br/>activities</th>\n        <td style=\"width: 41%;\">Government can restrict use of funds to authorized purposes</td>\n        <td style=\"width: 41%;\">\"Grant monies must be used for the acquisition, construction, and maintenance of appropriate performance facilities\"</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th>Funding<br/>recipients</th>\n        <td>Government cannot restrict protected conduct unrelated to funding's purpose</td>\n        <td>\"Recipient must agree to refrain from all kinds of political lobbying calculated to secure additional tax support for the performing arts\"</td>\n      </tr>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>The last section of the statute conditions state funding on a recipient's agreement to refrain from certain political lobbying efforts. Since this condition interferes with the First Amendment right to free expression—which is applied to the states through the Fourteenth Amendment—the section can be challenged on that basis. But due to the government's countervailing right to decide how to spend its funds, the success of this attack depends on whether the condition is placed on:</p>\n\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>funded activities</strong> – in which case, the government can insist that the funds be used for authorized purposes or</li>\n    <li><strong>funding recipients</strong> – in which case, the government cannot restrict the recipient's right to engage in protected conduct that falls outside the funding's purpose or scope (as seen here).</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <p>Political lobbying is protected First Amendment conduct that is unrelated to the activities—acquiring, constructing, and maintaining performing arts facilities—that are funded by the statute. And since the statute conditions the award of such grants on the recipient's agreement to refrain from such conduct, the First and Fourteenth Amendments provide the strongest constitutional basis to attack this section of the statute.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice-block-wrong\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice A)</strong> The <span style=\"color:#1a73e8;\">commerce clause</span> bars states from discriminating against interstate commerce by favoring in-state over out-of-state economic interests unless the state acts as a market participant (eg, by providing grants—as seen here). Therefore, this is a weak basis to attack the last section's constitutionality.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-choice-block-wrong\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\"><strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c;\">(Choice B)</strong> The <span style=\"color:#1a73e8;\">Fifth Amendment</span> does not, by itself, provide a basis to attack the last section since the Fifth Amendment only applies to the states through the Fourteenth Amendment.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n    <p>The government can condition funding on the promise that the funds be used for a particular purpose. But it cannot condition funding on a recipient's promise to refrain from engaging in protected First Amendment conduct if that conduct is unrelated to the funding's purpose or scope.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n    <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n      <li>Agency for Int'l Dev. v. All. for Open Soc'y Int'l, Inc., 570 U.S. 205, 221 (2013) (holding that a state funding program violated the First Amendment by conditioning funds on requirements unrelated to the program's purpose).</li>\n      <li>Rust v. Sullivan, 500 U.S. 173, 192–200 (1991) (upholding a federal funding program that limited fund recipients' ability to provide abortion-related services that were outside the program's scope).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一部州法规定，向位于该州的私立舞蹈、戏剧和歌剧团体提供州政府的资金补助。该法规定，此类补助金的受领人必须将所获资金用于购置、建造和维护适合其表演艺术公开演出的设施。该法的最后一节规定，每笔此类补助金的授予，都以受领人同意不进行任何旨在为表演艺术争取额外税收支持的政治游说为条件。\n\n以下哪项为质疑该法最后一节的有效性提供了最有力的宪法依据？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "商业条款。",
        "B": "第五修正案。",
        "C": "第一和第十四修正案。",
        "D": "合同义务条款。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    <title>MBE 解析：政府资助与言论自由</title>\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #e8f4f8;\r\n            --text-color: #333;\r\n            --bg-color: #f4f6f7;\r\n            --card-bg: #ffffff;\r\n            --border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: var(--bg-color);\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px; /* 适配手机逻辑宽度 */\r\n            width: 100%;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .card {\r\n            background-color: var(--card-bg);\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 16px;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header {\r\n            background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        h2 {\r\n            margin-top: 0;\r\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-bottom: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        h3 {\r\n            font-size: 1.1rem;\r\n            color: var(--accent-color);\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n            font-weight: 500;\r\n            margin: 10px 0;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .english-term {\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            font-size: 0.9em;\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .concept-box {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            border: 1px solid #ffeeba;\r\n            color: #856404;\r\n            padding: 12px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            margin-top: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        ul {\r\n            padding-left: 20px;\r\n            margin: 10px 0;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        li {\r\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .wrong-option {\r\n            opacity: 0.8;\r\n            font-size: 0.95rem;\r\n        }\r\n        \r\n        .badge {\r\n            display: inline-block;\r\n            padding: 2px 8px;\r\n            background-color: var(--accent-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            font-size: 0.8rem;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n\r\n    <!-- 标题区 -->\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <div style=\"font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.9;\">MBE 宪法考点解析</div>\r\n        <div style=\"font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold;\">违宪条件原则与政府资助</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 核心答案 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <span class=\"badge\">正确答案</span>\r\n        <h2>选项 C：第一和第十四修正案</h2>\r\n        <p>这是最有力的宪法攻击依据。本题的核心考点是<b>违宪条件原则 (Unconstitutional Conditions Doctrine)</b>。</p>\r\n        <div class=\"highlight\">\r\n            结论：政府不能通过“资助”作为诱饵，迫使受领人放弃其受宪法保护的言论自由权利（如政治游说），特别是当该限制与资助项目的范围无关时。\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 法律原理解析 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card\">\r\n        <h2>⚖️ 法律推理深度解析</h2>\r\n        \r\n        <h3>1. 权利基础 (The Right)</h3>\r\n        <p>政治游说 (Political Lobbying) 属于核心的政治言论，受到<b>第一修正案 (First Amendment)</b> 的最高级别保护。</p>\r\n\r\n        <h3>2. 法律适用 (Incorporation)</h3>\r\n        <p>由于本题涉及的是<b>州法律 (State Statute)</b>，第一修正案对联邦政府的限制必须通过<b>第十四修正案 (Fourteenth Amendment)</b> 的正当程序条款 (Due Process Clause) “纳入” (Incorporated) 从而适用于各州。因此，选项必须同时提及这两者。</p>\r\n\r\n        <h3>3. 核心考点：资助的界限</h3>\r\n        <p>MBE 经常考察政府资助权力的边界。请记住以下区分：</p>\r\n        \r\n        <div class=\"concept-box\">\r\n            <strong>✅ 政府可以限制资金用途 (Subsidized Activities)：</strong><br>\r\n            政府可以说：“这笔钱只能用来盖楼，不能用来游说。”<br>\r\n            <span class=\"english-term\">Government can define the limits of the government-funded program.</span>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <br>\r\n        <div class=\"concept-box\" style=\"background-color: #f8d7da; color: #721c24; border-color: #f5c6cb;\">\r\n            <strong>❌ 政府不能限制受领人本身 (The Recipient)：</strong><br>\r\n            政府不能说：“如果你拿了盖楼的钱，你就永远不能用你自己的钱去游说。”<br>\r\n            <span class=\"english-term\">Government cannot condition funding on the recipient's waiver of constitutional rights outside the scope of the program.</span>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p><strong>本案分析：</strong> 州法不仅限制了补助金的使用，还要求受领人同意“不进行任何旨在争取税收支持的政治游说”。这限制了受领人在资助项目之外的言论自由，构成了违宪条件。</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 错误选项分析 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card wrong-option\">\r\n        <h2>🚫 为什么其他选项是错的？</h2>\r\n        \r\n        <p><strong>A. 商业条款 (Commerce Clause)</strong><br>\r\n        虽然通常州不能歧视州际商业，但这里有一个重要例外：<b>市场参与者例外 (Market Participant Exception)</b>。当州政府作为买家或资助者（花自己的钱）时，它可以偏袒本州居民或团体。因此，这不是一个强有力的攻击点。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><strong>B. 第五修正案 (Fifth Amendment)</strong><br>\r\n        这是一个程序性陷阱。第五修正案直接约束<b>联邦政府</b>。要约束<b>州政府</b>，必须通过第十四修正案。单独引用第五修正案是法律依据上的错误。</p>\r\n\r\n        <p><strong>D. 合同义务条款 (Contracts Clause)</strong><br>\r\n        该条款禁止州通过法律实质性地损害<b>现有的 (Existing)</b> 合同义务。本案中，政府是提供新的资助协议，并没有废除或改变之前的合同，因此该条款不适用。</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n    <div class=\"card\" style=\"border-left-color: #e67e22;\">\r\n        <h3>💡 MBE 考试技巧</h3>\r\n        <p>当你看到题目涉及<b>“政府福利/资助” (Government Benefit/Grant)</b> 附带了<b>“放弃某项权利” (Condition requiring waiver of rights)</b> 时：</p>\r\n        <ol>\r\n            <li>首先检查该条件是否限制了<b>言论自由 (Free Speech)</b>。</li>\r\n            <li>判断该限制是仅针对<b>资金的使用</b>（通常允许），还是针对<b>受领人的所有活动</b>（通常违宪）。</li>\r\n            <li>如果是州政府的行为，确保答案包含<b>第十四修正案</b>。</li>\r\n        </ol>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
