    {
      "index": 34,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Regulation of speech",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "Members of a religious group believe in Lucifer as their Supreme Being. The members of this group meet once a year on top of a mountain, located in a national park, to hold an overnight encampment and a midnight dance around a large campfire. They believe that this overnight encampment and ritual are required by Lucifer to be held on the top of that mountain. U.S. National Park Service rules that have been consistently enforced prohibit all overnight camping and all campfires on the mountain because of the very great dangers overnight camping and campfires would pose in that particular location. As a result, the park superintendent denied a request by the religious group for a permit to conduct these activities on top of the mountain. The park superintendent, who was known to be violently opposed to cults and other unconventional groups, had previously issued permits to conventional religious groups to conduct sunrise services in other areas of that national park.\nThe religious group brought suit in federal court against the U.S. National Park Service and the superintendent of the park to compel issuance of the requested permit.\nAs a matter of constitutional law, was the denial of the permit valid?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because the free exercise clause of the First Amendment prohibits the Park Service from knowingly interfering with religious conduct.",
        "B": "No, because these facts demonstrate that the action of the Park Service purposefully and invidiously discriminated against the religious group.",
        "C": "Yes, because religiously motivated conduct may be subjected to nondiscriminatory time, place, and manner restrictions that advance important public interests.",
        "D": "Yes, because the establishment clause of the First Amendment prohibits the holding of religious ceremonies on federal land."
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0034.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      color: #1f1f1f;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation {\n      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      max-width: 100%;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation * {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation p {\n      margin: 0 0 1em 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-center {\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-wrap {\n      margin: 1.2rem 0 1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-scroll-x {\n      overflow-x: auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;\n      margin: 16px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-inner {\n      min-width: 760px;\n      padding: 0.5rem 0.25rem 0.75rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-top {\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      margin-bottom: 1.8rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-pill {\n      display: inline-block;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border-radius: 1rem;\n      padding: 0.45rem 1.2rem;\n      box-shadow: 0 0.18rem 0.45rem rgba(0,0,0,0.18);\n      border: 1px solid #e5e5e5;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      font-size: 1.15rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch {\n      position: relative;\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n      gap: 2rem;\n      align-items: start;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch::before {\n      content: \"\";\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 50%;\n      top: -1rem;\n      width: 0;\n      height: 1rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      transform: translateX(-1px);\n    }\n    .pbx-branch::after {\n      content: \"\";\n      position: absolute;\n      left: 18%;\n      top: -0.1rem;\n      width: 64%;\n      border-top: 2px solid #555;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch-col {\n      position: relative;\n      padding-top: 1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch-col::before {\n      content: \"\";\n      position: absolute;\n      top: -0.1rem;\n      left: 50%;\n      width: 0;\n      height: 1rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      transform: translateX(-1px);\n    }\n    .pbx-branch-col.left::after,\n    .pbx-branch-col.right::after {\n      content: \"\";\n      position: absolute;\n      top: -0.1rem;\n      left: 50%;\n      width: 0;\n      height: 1rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      transform: translateX(-1px);\n    }\n    .pbx-box {\n      display: block;\n      width: 100%;\n      background: #f7f7f7;\n      border-radius: 0.9rem;\n      padding: 1rem 1.2rem;\n      box-shadow: 0 0.15rem 0.4rem rgba(0,0,0,0.12);\n      border: 1px solid #efefef;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.35;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-box strong {\n      font-size: 1.08rem;\n      display: block;\n      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-box .pbx-small {\n      font-size: 0.97rem;\n      line-height: 1.35;\n    }\n    .pbx-box ul {\n      margin: 0.4rem 0 0;\n      padding-left: 1.2rem;\n      text-align: left;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-mid {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n      gap: 2rem;\n      margin-top: 2.1rem;\n      align-items: start;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-bottom {\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      margin-top: 1.8rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-connector {\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      margin: 0.3rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-down {\n      width: 0;\n      height: 1.1rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      position: relative;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-down::after {\n      content: \"\";\n      position: absolute;\n      left: -0.35rem;\n      bottom: -0.05rem;\n      width: 0.5rem;\n      height: 0.5rem;\n      border-left: 2px solid #555;\n      border-bottom: 2px solid #555;\n      transform: rotate(-45deg);\n    }\n    .pbx-text {\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-text strong { font-weight: 700; }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding-left: 18px;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      color: #555;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body {\n        font-size: 0.95rem;\n        padding: 0.75rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-explanation {\n        padding: 0.875rem 1rem;\n      }\n      .pbx-pill { font-size: 1.03rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-inner { min-width: 760px; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- pbx-topic: Regulation of speech -->\n  <div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-flow-wrap\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-scroll-x\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-inner\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-top\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-pill\">Free speech analysis</div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-branch\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-branch-col left\">\n              <div class=\"pbx-box\">\n                <strong>Content-based restriction</strong>\n                <div class=\"pbx-small\">(message, subject, or idea)</div>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-connector\"><div class=\"pbx-arrow-down\"></div></div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-box\">\n                <strong>Strict scrutiny</strong>\n                <div class=\"pbx-small\">(least restrictive means)</div>\n                <ul>\n                  <li>Necessary &amp; narrowly tailored to compelling interest</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"pbx-branch-col right\">\n              <div class=\"pbx-box\">\n                <strong>Content-neutral restriction</strong>\n                <div class=\"pbx-small\">(time, place, or manner)</div>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-connector\"><div class=\"pbx-arrow-down\"></div></div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-box\">\n                <strong>Intermediate scrutiny</strong>\n                <div class=\"pbx-small\">(no greater than necessary)</div>\n                <ul>\n                  <li>Narrowly tailored to substantial interest</li>\n                  <li>Alternative avenues of communication</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-bottom\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-box\" style=\"max-width: 22rem;\">\n              <strong>Exception</strong>\n              <div class=\"pbx-small\">(nonpublic forum + viewpoint-neutral)</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-bottom\" style=\"margin-top: 0.8rem;\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-arrow-down\"></div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-bottom\">\n            <div class=\"pbx-box\" style=\"max-width: 18rem;\">\n              <strong>Rational basis</strong>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Reasonably related to legitimate interest</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-text\">\n      <p>The permit denial restricts the religious group's right to free expression by preventing its religiously motivated conduct. However, the permit was denied because of a content-neutral (ie, nondiscriminatory) rule prohibiting all overnight camping and campfires on the mountain—not because of the content of the group's religious conduct. As a result, this time, place, or manner restriction is valid under intermediate scrutiny if it:</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>is narrowly tailored (ie, no greater than necessary) to serve a substantial or important government interest and</li>\n        <li>leaves open ample alternative channels of communication.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The park has an important interest in avoiding the \"very great dangers\" posed by overnight camping and campfires. And the park rule is narrowly tailored to that interest since (1) park safety would be compromised by allowing the prohibited activities and (2) there is no evidence that the group's conduct poses no such safety threat. The rule also provides alternative channels of communication since the group can conduct religious rituals at other times and places. Therefore, this speech restriction is valid.</p>\n\n      <p>The permit denial also interferes with the group's right to free exercise of religion, which largely prohibits intentional government interference with religion (<span style=\"color:#9b1c1c;font-weight:600;\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\">Choice A</span>). But an incidental interference is permissible if it is rationally related to a legitimate government interest. Here, the permit was denied under a generally applicable park rule (not the superintendent's beliefs), so the religious interference was incidental. And since the rule is rationally related to a legitimate interest in park safety, the permit denial complied with this right (<span style=\"color:#9b1c1c;font-weight:600;\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\">Choice B</span>).</p>\n\n      <p><strong>(Choice D)</strong> The establishment clause prohibits the government from favoring a particular religion or religion generally. Therefore, religious ceremonies on federal land are permissible so long as the government remains neutral toward religion.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n        <p>First Amendment free speech protections extend to religious conduct. But the government can impose content-neutral restrictions on such conduct so long as they (1) are narrowly tailored to serve an important government interest and (2) leave open ample alternative channels of communication.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n        <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n          <li>Clark v. Cmty. for Creative Non-Violence, 468 U.S. 288, 298–99 (1984) (holding that the denial of a camping permit for a demonstration is a constitutional time, place, and manner restriction on speech).</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一个宗教团体的成员信仰 Lucifer 为其至高无上的神。该团体的成员每年一次在一个国家公园内的山顶上聚会，举行通宵露营和围绕大篝火的午夜舞蹈。他们相信，Lucifer 要求他们在该山顶上举行这种通宵露营和仪式。U.S. National Park Service 的规定一贯禁止在该山上进行任何通宵露营和篝火，因为通宵露营和篝火在该特定地点会造成极大的危险。因此，公园负责人拒绝了该宗教团体在该山顶上进行这些活动的许可申请。该公园负责人以强烈反对邪教和其他非传统团体而闻名，此前曾向传统宗教团体颁发许可，允许其在该国家公园的其他区域举行日出仪式。\n\n该宗教团体在联邦法院对 U.S. National Park Service 和该公园负责人提起诉讼，要求强制颁发所申请的许可。\n\n从宪法角度看，拒绝颁发该许可的行为是否有效？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "否，因为第一修正案的自由行使条款禁止公园管理局故意干涉宗教行为。",
        "B": "否，因为这些事实表明，公园管理局的行为是蓄意地、不公正地歧视该宗教团体。",
        "C": "是，因为出于宗教动机的行为可能会受到非歧视性的时间、地点和方式限制，以促进重要的公共利益。",
        "D": "是，因为第一修正案的政教分离条款禁止在联邦土地上举行宗教仪式。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        body {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            background-color: #f4f6f8;\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            color: #333;\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            margin: 0 auto;\r\n            background: #ffffff;\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n        .header {\r\n            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2c3e50, #4ca1af);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .header h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n            font-weight: 700;\r\n        }\r\n        .header p {\r\n            margin: 5px 0 0;\r\n            font-size: 12px;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n        }\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-box {\r\n            background-color: #e8f5e9;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid #4caf50;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-title {\r\n            color: #2e7d32;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            font-size: 16px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-card {\r\n            background-color: #fff;\r\n            border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: #1976d2;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .concept-title::before {\r\n            content: \"⚖️\";\r\n            margin-right: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            padding: 2px 4px;\r\n            border-radius: 3px;\r\n            font-weight: 500;\r\n        }\r\n        .trap-alert {\r\n            background-color: #ffebee;\r\n            border: 1px solid #ffcdd2;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .trap-title {\r\n            color: #c62828;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n            font-size: 14px;\r\n        }\r\n        ul {\r\n            padding-left: 20px;\r\n            margin: 5px 0;\r\n        }\r\n        li {\r\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        .footer {\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            background-color: #f8f9fa;\r\n            font-size: 12px;\r\n            color: #666;\r\n            border-top: 1px solid #eee;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <p>宪法第一修正案：宗教行为与政府管制</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 正确答案部分 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n            <div class=\"answer-title\">✅ 正确答案：选项 C</div>\r\n            <p>是的，因为出于宗教动机的行为可能会受到<b>非歧视性的时间、地点和方式限制 (Time, Place, and Manner Restrictions)</b>，以促进重要的公共利益。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 核心考点解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\">核心考点：中度审查标准</div>\r\n            <p>虽然第一修正案保护宗教自由和言论自由，但政府可以对公共场所的行为进行管制。如果管制是<b>内容中立 (Content-Neutral)</b> 的，法院将适用<b>中度审查 (Intermediate Scrutiny)</b>。</p>\r\n            <hr style=\"border: 0; border-top: 1px dashed #ccc; margin: 10px 0;\">\r\n            <p><b>有效限制的三要素：</b></p>\r\n            <ul>\r\n                <li><b>内容中立：</b> 规则必须适用于所有人，无论其言论或宗教内容如何（本题中禁止<i>所有</i>露营）。</li>\r\n                <li><b>重大的政府利益 (Significant Government Interest)：</b> 政府必须有正当理由（本题中是为了防止“极大危险”和维护公园安全）。</li>\r\n                <li><b>狭义定制 (Narrowly Tailored) 且保留替代渠道：</b> 限制手段不能过宽，且必须允许人们通过其他方式表达（本题中可以在其他时间/地点进行）。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 判例关联 -->\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\">经典判例关联</div>\r\n            <p>本题的情境直接对应最高法院的经典判例 <span class=\"highlight\">Clark v. Community for Creative Non-Violence (1984)</span>。</p>\r\n            <p>在该案中，法院裁定国家公园管理局禁止在 Lafayette Park 露营睡觉的规定是有效的，即使示威者声称露营是他们抗议无家可归问题的“表达行为”。法院认为该禁令是合理的时间、地点和方式限制。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 陷阱排除 -->\r\n        <div class=\"trap-alert\">\r\n            <div class=\"trap-title\">⚠️ 常见陷阱：官员的个人偏见 (Option B)</div>\r\n            <p>很多考生会误选 <b>选项 B</b>，因为题目提到公园负责人“强烈反对邪教”。</p>\r\n            <p><b>为什么 B 是错的？</b><br>\r\n            虽然负责人有偏见，但拒绝许可的依据是<b>一贯执行的、普遍适用的规则 (Consistently Enforced Rule)</b>，该规则禁止<i>所有人</i>在该特定危险区域露营。如果规则本身是中立的并且被平等地执行，官员的内心动机通常不会使该行为违宪。</p>\r\n            <p>此外，其他团体获得的许可是针对“其他区域”和“日出仪式”（非通宵露营），因此不存在针对该团体的歧视性待遇。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\" style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; border: none;\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-title\" style=\"color: #555;\">其他选项分析</div>\r\n            <ul style=\"font-size: 13px;\">\r\n                <li><b>选项 A (Free Exercise)：</b> 错误。宗教信仰自由是绝对的，但<b>宗教行为 (Religious Conduct)</b> 不是。普遍适用的刑法或安全法规（如禁止在危险山顶生火）通常可以限制宗教行为 (<i>Employment Division v. Smith</i>)。</li>\r\n                <li><b>选项 D (Establishment Clause)：</b> 错误。政教分离条款并不禁止在联邦土地上进行<i>所有</i>宗教仪式。只要政府保持中立，不偏袒特定宗教，公共场所是可以用于宗教表达的。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n        </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"footer\">\r\n        MBE Constitutional Law Review<br>\r\n        Focus: First Amendment / Time, Place, and Manner\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
