    {
      "index": 35,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Regulation of speech",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A public university requires students to pay a student-activity fee that funds the activities of various student organizations. The university allocates these funds to student organizations without regard to their views.\nA student organization received student-activity fee funds to hold a float parade. The organization rejected a student's float submission because the views espoused by the float were contrary to the organization's and parade's message. The student appealed the organization's decision to the university, but the university upheld the rejection of his submission.\nThe student has filed an action against the university, arguing that the university's decision to uphold the organization's rejection of the student's submission and the university's mandatory student-activity fee violate the First Amendment.\nAre the university's actions constitutional?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "The decision to uphold the organization's rejection of the student's submission and the mandatory student-activity fee are constitutional.",
        "B": "The decision to uphold the organization's rejection of the student's submission and the mandatory student-activity fee are unconstitutional.",
        "C": "The decision to uphold the organization's rejection of the student's submission is constitutional but the mandatory student-activity fee is unconstitutional.",
        "D": "The decision to uphold the organization's rejection of the student's submission is unconstitutional but the mandatory student-activity fee is constitutional."
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0035.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      color: #111;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation {\n      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      max-width: 100%;\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      word-break: break-word;\n      overflow-wrap: break-word;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation p {\n      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-title {\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 1.5rem;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-scroll-x {\n      overflow-x: auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;\n      margin: 1rem 0;\n    }\n    table {\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n      border-collapse: collapse;\n      width: 100%;\n      min-width: 480px;\n    }\n    th, td {\n      border: 1px solid #cccccc;\n      padding: 8px 12px;\n      vertical-align: top;\n      font-size: 1rem;\n    }\n    th {\n      background: #f5f5f5;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n    .pbx-table-head {\n      background: #fff;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 1.15rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-table-type {\n      width: 26%;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      vertical-align: middle;\n      font-size: 1.05rem;\n    }\n    ul {\n      margin: 0.25rem 0 0.75rem 1.5rem;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n    li {\n      margin: 0.2rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding-left: 18px;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      color: #555;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list li {\n      margin: 0.2rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-note {\n      margin-top: 0.5rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-small {\n      font-size: 0.95rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-strong {\n      font-weight: 700;\n    }\n    .pbx-italic {\n      font-style: italic;\n    }\n    @media (max-width: 640px) {\n      body { font-size: 0.95rem; padding: 0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation { padding: 0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-title { font-size: 1.25rem; }\n      th, td { font-size: 0.825rem; padding: 0.5em 0.625em; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- pbx-topic: Regulation of speech -->\n<div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n  <div class=\"pbx-scroll-x\">\n    <table>\n      <tr>\n        <th colspan=\"2\" class=\"pbx-table-head\">First Amendment freedom not to speak</th>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <th style=\"width:26%;\">Type</th>\n        <th>Examples</th>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td class=\"pbx-table-type\">Impermissible<br/>compulsion</td>\n        <td>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Forcing students to salute flag or recite Pledge of Allegiance</li>\n            <li>Punishing motorists for covering state motto on license plates</li>\n            <li>Requiring private groups to include opposing viewpoints in their events</li>\n            <li>Requiring nonunion employees to pay public-sector union dues</li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td class=\"pbx-table-type\">Permissible<br/>compulsion</td>\n        <td>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Forcing public university students to pay activity fee if funds allocated in viewpoint-neutral manner</li>\n            <li>Requiring public shopping center to permit speech on property if speech not dictated by state &amp; not identified with center's owner</li>\n            <li>Requiring lawyers to join bar association &amp; pay dues to practice law</li>\n          </ul>\n        </td>\n      </tr>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <p>The First Amendment protects individuals' freedom to speak and their freedom not to speak. This means that the government and its subsidiaries (eg, public universities) <strong>cannot compel individuals to endorse or include viewpoints with which they disagree.</strong> Here, the student organization had the right to reject the student's float submission, and the university could not force the organization to accept that submission. Therefore, the university's decision to uphold the organization's rejection of the submission is constitutional <strong>(Choices B &amp; D).</strong></p>\n\n  <p>Additionally, the First Amendment <strong>generally prohibits</strong> the government and its subsidiaries from <strong>compelling individuals to financially support private speech</strong> with which they disagree.* However, there are limited <strong>exceptions</strong> to this rule, including that a public university can force its students to pay a student-activity fee if the funds are allocated in a <strong>viewpoint-neutral manner.</strong> Since the public university here allocates funds to student organizations without regard to their views, the mandatory student-activity fee is constitutional <strong>(Choices B &amp; C).</strong></p>\n\n  <p class=\"pbx-small pbx-italic\">*Individuals can be compelled to subsidize government speech through taxes because the First Amendment does not prohibit the government from using taxpayer funds to advocate for or defend its own policies or viewpoints.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n    <p>The First Amendment protects the right to speak and not to speak. This means that the government cannot compel individuals to endorse, include, or financially support private speech with which they disagree. However, a public university can compel its students to pay an activity fee if the funds are allocated in a viewpoint-neutral manner.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n    <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n      <li>Hurley v. Irish-Am. Gay, Lesbian &amp; Bisexual Grp. of Bos., 515 U.S. 557, 581 (1995) (holding that a state may not require private parade organizers to include messages they oppose in the parade).</li>\n      <li>Bd. of Regents of Univ. of Wisconsin Sys. v. Southworth, 529 U.S. 217, 234 (2000) (holding that a public university's mandatory student-activity fee is constitutional if the fee is allocated in a viewpoint-neutral manner).</li>\n      <li>16A Am. Jur. 2d Constitutional Law §§ 471–73 (2020) (explaining when the First Amendment prohibits government-compelled speech).</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一所公立大学要求学生支付学生活动费，用于资助各类学生组织的活动。该大学在分配这些资金给学生组织时，不考虑其观点。\n\n一个学生组织收到了学生活动费资金，用于举办花车游行。该组织拒绝了一名学生提交的花车方案，因为该花车所支持的观点与该组织及游行所要传达的信息相悖。该学生就该组织的决定向大学提出上诉，但大学维持了拒绝其方案的决定。\n\n该学生对大学提起诉讼，主张大学维持该组织拒绝其方案的决定以及大学强制征收学生活动费的行为违反了 First Amendment（第一修正案）。\n\n该大学的行为是否合宪？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "维持该组织拒绝学生方案的决定以及强制征收学生活动费的行为均合宪。",
        "B": "维持该组织拒绝学生方案的决定以及强制征收学生活动费的行为均违宪。",
        "C": "维持该组织拒绝学生方案的决定合宪，但强制征收学生活动费的行为违宪。",
        "D": "维持该组织拒绝学生方案的决定违宪，但强制征收学生活动费的行为合宪。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --success-color: #27ae60;\r\n            --warning-color: #f39c12;\r\n            --bg-color: #f4f6f7;\r\n            --card-bg: #ffffff;\r\n            --text-color: #333333;\r\n        }\r\n        \r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: var(--bg-color);\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px; /* 适配手机屏幕 */\r\n            width: 100%;\r\n            background-color: var(--card-bg);\r\n            border-radius: 12px;\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header {\r\n            background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .header .subtitle {\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .answer-box {\r\n            background-color: #e8f6f3;\r\n            border-left: 5px solid var(--success-color);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 4px;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .answer-title {\r\n            color: var(--success-color);\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n            display: block;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .section-title {\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            font-size: 1.1rem;\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding-bottom: 5px;\r\n            margin-top: 25px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .concept-card {\r\n            background-color: #fff;\r\n            border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\r\n            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .concept-header {\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            align-items: center;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--accent-color);\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .icon {\r\n            margin-right: 8px;\r\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .highlight {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            padding: 2px 4px;\r\n            border-radius: 3px;\r\n            font-weight: 500;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        table {\r\n            width: 100%;\r\n            border-collapse: collapse;\r\n            margin: 15px 0;\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        th, td {\r\n            border: 1px solid #ddd;\r\n            padding: 8px;\r\n            text-align: left;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        th {\r\n            background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .case-ref {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #7f8c8d;\r\n            font-size: 0.85rem;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n            display: block;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .exam-tip {\r\n            background-color: #fff8e1;\r\n            border: 1px dashed var(--warning-color);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: 8px;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n            font-size: 0.95rem;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        .footer {\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            font-size: 0.8rem;\r\n            color: #999;\r\n            border-top: 1px solid #eee;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <div class=\"subtitle\">Constitutional Law - First Amendment</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 答案部分 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-box\">\r\n            <span class=\"answer-title\">正确答案：A</span>\r\n            大学维持组织拒绝学生方案的决定，以及强制征收学生活动费的行为，<b>均为合宪</b>。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p>本题考察第一修正案（First Amendment）中的两个核心概念：<b>不言论的自由（Freedom Not to Speak）</b>与<b>强制资助言论（Compelled Subsidy）</b>。</p>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考点一 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">考点一：私人团体的言论控制权</div>\r\n        \r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-header\">\r\n                <span class=\"icon\">📢</span>\r\n                <span>游行是表达性行为</span>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <p>游行（Parade）被视为一种表达性行为。私人组织者有权决定其游行想要传达的信息。</p>\r\n            <p>根据第一修正案，政府（此处为公立大学）<b>不能强迫</b>私人团体在其表达性活动中包含与其信息相悖的观点。这属于“不言论的自由”。</p>\r\n            <span class=\"case-ref\">关联判例：Hurley v. Irish-American Gay, Lesbian & Bisexual Group of Boston (1995)</span>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>本案分析：</b>学生组织有权拒绝该学生的花车，因为该花车传达的观点与组织相悖。如果大学强迫该组织接受该花车，反而是大学侵犯了该组织的言论自由。因此，大学<b>维持拒绝决定</b>是合宪的。</p>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考点二 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">考点二：强制性学生活动费</div>\r\n\r\n        <div class=\"concept-card\">\r\n            <div class=\"concept-header\">\r\n                <span class=\"icon\">💰</span>\r\n                <span>观点中立原则 (Viewpoint Neutrality)</span>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <p>通常，政府不能强迫个人出资支持其反对的私人言论。但在公立大学环境中有一个重要<b>例外</b>：</p>\r\n            <p>只要资金分配是<b>观点中立（Viewpoint-Neutral）</b>的，即不基于组织的政治或意识形态倾向来分配资金，大学就可以强制收取学生活动费。</p>\r\n            <span class=\"case-ref\">关联判例：Board of Regents of Univ. of Wisconsin System v. Southworth (2000)</span>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <p><b>本案分析：</b>题目明确指出大学在分配资金时“不考虑其观点”（without regard to their views）。因此，强制收费旨在促进校园内的“思想市场”（Marketplace of Ideas），是合宪的。</p>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 对比表格 -->\r\n        <div class=\"section-title\">强迫行为的合宪性对比</div>\r\n        <table>\r\n            <tr>\r\n                <th>类型</th>\r\n                <th>是否合宪</th>\r\n                <th>关键理由</th>\r\n            </tr>\r\n            <tr>\r\n                <td><b>强迫参与游行</b><br>(Compelled Speech)</td>\r\n                <td>❌ 违宪</td>\r\n                <td>侵犯了组织者自主决定信息的权利 (Hurley案)。</td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n            <tr>\r\n                <td><b>强制学生活动费</b><br>(Compelled Subsidy)</td>\r\n                <td>✅ 合宪</td>\r\n                <td>前提是资金分配必须<b>观点中立</b> (Southworth案)。</td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n            <tr>\r\n                <td><b>强制工会会费</b><br>(Public Sector Unions)</td>\r\n                <td>❌ 违宪</td>\r\n                <td>强迫非会员资助工会的政治游说违反第一修正案 (Janus案)。</td>\r\n            </tr>\r\n        </table>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        <div class=\"exam-tip\">\r\n            <strong>🎓 MBE 考试技巧：</strong>\r\n            <br><br>\r\n            看到“公立大学”+“学生活动费”（Student Activity Fee）的组合时，立即寻找<b>“Viewpoint Neutral”（观点中立）</b>这个关键词。\r\n            <ul>\r\n                <li>如果分配是中立的 ➡️ <b>合宪</b>。</li>\r\n                <li>如果分配偏向某一立场 ➡️ <b>违宪</b>。</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n            同时，切记私人组织（即使接受资助）仍保留拒绝与其理念不符的言论的权利。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    \r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
