    {
      "index": 39,
      "subject": "Constitutional Law",
      "chapter": "Individual Rights",
      "topic": "Obligation of contracts",
      "count": 120,
      "question": "A state in which several popular ski resorts are located has enacted a law requiring state certification of ski instructors. Under the law, applicants for certification must attend a monthlong course, pass a test, and pay a fee of $1,000. The stated purpose of the law is to \"promote uniformity in the methods of ski instruction at the state's ski areas.\"\nShortly before the law's enactment, when the state did not require certification of ski instructors, a woman moved to the state intending to find employment as a ski instructor. The woman had been a ski instructor in another state for many years. But since her move, even though ski resorts in the state have found her to be highly qualified, no resort will offer her a contract for employment as a ski instructor because she has not received the required state certification.\nAs applied to the woman, does the state certification requirement constitute a violation of the contracts clause?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "No, because her ability to contract for employment with the state is not being impaired.",
        "B": "No, because she has no existing contract that is being impaired.",
        "C": "Yes, because as applied to an otherwise qualified ski instructor, the requirement is not rationally related to a legitimate government interest.",
        "D": "Yes, because the requirement substantially impairs her ability to contract for employment in the absence of an important government objective."
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "source_img": "source_imgs/q0039.png",
      "explanation": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Explanation</title>\n  <style>\n    body{\n      margin:0;\n      font-size:1rem;\n      line-height:1.7;\n      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      color:#111;\n      background:#fff;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation{\n      padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;\n      box-sizing:border-box;\n      max-width:100%;\n      overflow-wrap:break-word;\n      word-break:break-word;\n    }\n    .pbx-explanation *{ box-sizing:border-box; }\n    .pbx-center{ text-align:center; }\n    .pbx-title{\n      font-size:1.9rem;\n      font-weight:700;\n      text-align:center;\n      margin:0 0 1.25rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-wrap{\n      margin:0.5rem auto 1.25rem auto;\n      width:100%;\n      overflow-x:auto;\n      -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;\n      padding-bottom:0.25rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-inner{\n      min-width: 48rem;\n      max-width: 100%;\n      margin:0 auto;\n      position:relative;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-step{\n      display:inline-block;\n      position:relative;\n      background:#fff;\n      border-radius:1rem;\n      box-shadow:0 0.18rem 0.45rem rgba(0,0,0,0.12);\n      border:1px solid #f0f0f0;\n      padding:0.75rem 1rem;\n      text-align:center;\n      font-size:1.08rem;\n      line-height:1.35;\n      width:18rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-flow-step.small{ width:17rem; }\n    .pbx-flow-step.medium{ width:20rem; }\n    .pbx-flow-row{\n      display:flex;\n      justify-content:center;\n      align-items:center;\n      gap:1rem;\n      margin:0.75rem 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-right, .pbx-arrow-down, .pbx-arrow-branch{\n      position:relative;\n      font-size:1.05rem;\n      color:#222;\n      text-align:center;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-right::after{\n      content:\"\";\n      display:inline-block;\n      width:3.2rem;\n      border-top:1px solid #222;\n      vertical-align:middle;\n      margin-left:0.6rem;\n      position:relative;\n      top:-0.15rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-down{\n      height:1.8rem;\n      width:100%;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-down::before{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      left:50%;\n      top:0;\n      transform:translateX(-50%);\n      height:1.5rem;\n      border-left:1px solid #222;\n    }\n    .pbx-arrow-down::after{\n      content:\"↓\";\n      position:absolute;\n      left:50%;\n      top:0.88rem;\n      transform:translateX(-50%);\n      font-size:1.1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch{\n      position:relative;\n      width:100%;\n      height:3rem;\n      margin:0.2rem 0 0.1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch::before{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      left:50%;\n      top:0;\n      bottom:1.25rem;\n      border-left:1px solid #222;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch::after{\n      content:\"\";\n      position:absolute;\n      left:18%;\n      right:18%;\n      top:1.2rem;\n      border-top:1px solid #222;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch-label{\n      position:absolute;\n      top:-0.1rem;\n      left:50%;\n      transform:translateX(-50%);\n      font-size:1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch-no{\n      position:absolute;\n      right:11%;\n      top:-0.1rem;\n      font-size:1rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch-down{\n      position:absolute;\n      left:18%;\n      top:1.2rem;\n      width:1px;\n      height:1.8rem;\n      border-left:1px solid #222;\n    }\n    .pbx-branch-down.right{\n      left:auto;\n      right:18%;\n    }\n    .pbx-two-col{\n      display:flex;\n      justify-content:space-between;\n      gap:1.5rem;\n      margin-top:0.25rem;\n    }\n    .pbx-col{\n      flex:1;\n      display:flex;\n      justify-content:center;\n    }\n    .pbx-caption{\n      font-size:1.05rem;\n      text-align:center;\n      margin-top:0.3rem;\n      line-height:1.35;\n    }\n    .pbx-caption em{ font-style:italic; }\n    .pbx-note{\n      font-size:1rem;\n      margin-top:1rem;\n      line-height:1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-paragraph{\n      margin:0.9rem 0;\n      font-size:1rem;\n      line-height:1.75;\n    }\n    .pbx-paragraph strong{ font-weight:700; }\n    .pbx-edu-objective {\n      background: #f0f7ff;\n      border-left: 4px solid #3498db;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 24px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-edu-objective-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #2980b9;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-references {\n      background: #fafafa;\n      border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      padding: 14px 18px;\n      margin: 20px 0;\n    }\n    .pbx-references-title {\n      font-size: 13px;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      color: #555;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      letter-spacing: 0.05em;\n      margin-bottom: 8px;\n    }\n    .pbx-ref-list {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding-left: 18px;\n      font-size: 14px;\n      color: #555;\n      line-height: 1.7;\n    }\n    .pbx-small{ font-size:0.95em; }\n    @media (max-width: 640px){\n      body{ font-size:0.95rem; padding:0.75rem; }\n      .pbx-explanation{ padding:0.875rem 1rem; }\n      .pbx-title{ font-size:1.55rem; }\n      .pbx-flow-step{ font-size:1rem; }\n      .pbx-caption,.pbx-paragraph{ font-size:0.95rem; }\n      th, td{ font-size:0.825rem; padding:0.5em 0.625em; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- pbx-topic: Obligation of contracts -->\n  <div class=\"pbx-explanation\">\n    <div class=\"pbx-title\">Contracts clause analysis</div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-flow-wrap\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-flow-inner\">\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-row\" style=\"margin-top:0;\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-step medium\">Does plaintiff have existing contract?</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-arrow-right\" style=\"width:5rem; margin-top:1.2rem;\">No</div>\n          <div style=\"font-size:1.1rem; font-weight:700; margin-top:1.1rem;\">Constitutional</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-arrow-down\"></div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-row\" style=\"margin-top:0;\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-step medium\">Does new state law substantially<br/>impair contract?</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-arrow-right\" style=\"width:5rem; margin-top:1.2rem;\">No</div>\n          <div style=\"font-size:1.1rem; font-weight:700; margin-top:1.1rem;\">Constitutional</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-arrow-down\"></div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-branch\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-branch-label\">Yes</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-branch-down\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-branch-down right\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-two-col\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-col\">\n            <div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-step small\">Private contract<br/><span class=\"pbx-small\"><em>(more deference to state)</em></span></div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-col\">\n            <div>\n              <div class=\"pbx-flow-step small\">Public contract<br/><span class=\"pbx-small\"><em>(less deference to state)</em></span></div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-branch\" style=\"height:2.6rem; margin-top:0.3rem;\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-branch-down\" style=\"left:22%; top:0.25rem; height:1.8rem;\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-branch-down right\" style=\"right:22%; top:0.25rem; height:1.8rem;\"></div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-branch::after\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"pbx-arrow-down\" style=\"margin-top:-0.35rem;\"></div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-flow-row\" style=\"margin-top:0;\">\n          <div class=\"pbx-flow-step medium\">Is impairment reasonable &amp; narrowly tailored<br/>to important &amp; legitimate public interest?</div>\n          <div class=\"pbx-arrow-right\" style=\"width:5rem; margin-top:1.2rem;\">Yes</div>\n          <div style=\"font-size:1.1rem; font-weight:700; margin-top:1.1rem;\">Constitutional</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"pbx-arrow-down\"></div>\n        <div style=\"text-align:center; font-size:1.1rem; font-weight:700;\">Unconstitutional</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-note\">\n      The <strong>contracts clause</strong> restricts state laws—not court decisions or federal legislation—that substantially <strong>impair existing contracts</strong>. Therefore, this clause does not apply to <strong>future contracts</strong>.\n    </div>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-paragraph\">\n      Here, the state law interferes with the woman's ability to obtain an employment contract as a ski instructor. But since she has not been hired by a ski resort, the law does not impair any <strong>existing contract</strong>. Therefore, the state certification requirement does not violate the contracts clause <span style=\"color:#1f8f4d;font-weight:600;\" data-choice=\"B\" data-choice-role=\"correct\">as applied</span> to the woman.\n    </p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-paragraph\" data-choice=\"A\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\" style=\"border-left:3px solid #c0392b;padding-left:10px;\">\n      <strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choice A)</strong> The contracts clause applies to private contracts (ie, agreements with non-government parties) and public contracts (ie, agreements with government entities). But the woman's ability to contract for employment with the state is irrelevant since this clause only protects existing contracts.\n    </p>\n\n    <p class=\"pbx-paragraph\" data-choice=\"C D\" data-choice-role=\"distractor\">\n      <strong style=\"color:#9b1c1c\">(Choices C &amp; D)</strong> The contracts clause would only apply if the woman—qualified or not—had an existing contract. And had one existed, a substantial impairment of that contract would only be upheld if it was reasonable and narrowly tailored (not just rationally related) to an important and legitimate government interest (here, promoting uniformity in ski-instruction methods in the state).\n    </p>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-edu-objective-title\">📌 Educational Objective</div>\n      <p style=\"margin:0;\">The contracts clause restricts state laws that substantially impair existing (not future) contracts.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"pbx-references\">\n      <div class=\"pbx-references-title\">📚 References</div>\n      <ul class=\"pbx-ref-list\">\n        <li>U.S. Const. art. I, § 10 (contracts clause).</li>\n        <li>Gen. Motors Corp. v. Romein, 503 U.S. 181, 186 (1992) (explaining that the contracts clause only applies when a state law substantially impairs an existing contractual relationship).</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "zh-question": "一个拥有数个热门滑雪胜地的州颁布了一项法律，要求滑雪教练必须获得州级认证。根据该法律，申请认证者必须参加为期一个月的课程、通过一项考试并支付1000美元的费用。该法律宣称的目的是“促进本州滑雪区滑雪教学方法的一致性”。\n\n在该法律颁布前不久，当该州还不要求滑雪教练认证时，一名女子搬到该州，打算找一份滑雪教练的工作。这名女子在另一个州当了很多年的滑雪教练。但自从她搬来后，尽管该州的滑雪胜地认为她非常合格，却没有一家滑雪胜地愿意向她提供滑雪教练的雇佣合同，因为她没有获得所要求的州级认证。\n\n就适用于这名女子的情况而言，该州的认证要求是否构成了对合同条款的违反？",
      "zh-choices": {
        "A": "不会，因为她与州政府签订雇佣合同的能力并未受到损害。",
        "B": "不会，因为她没有现存的合同受到损害。",
        "C": "会，因为就适用于一名在其他方面合格的滑雪教练而言，该要求与合法的政府利益之间没有合理的关联。",
        "D": "会，因为在没有重要的政府目标的情况下，该要求严重损害了她签订雇佣合同的能力。"
      },
      "zh-explanation": "<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"zh-CN\">\r\n<head>\r\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n    \r\n    <style>\r\n        strong, b {\r\n            display: inline !important; \r\n            white-space: normal !important; \r\n            word-break: normal !important;\n            overflow-wrap: break-word !important;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n        :root {\r\n            --primary-color: #2c3e50;\r\n            --accent-color: #3498db;\r\n            --highlight-bg: #e8f4f8;\r\n            --text-color: #333;\r\n            --correct-color: #27ae60;\r\n            --wrong-color: #c0392b;\r\n            --border-radius: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        body {\r\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            background-color: #f4f7f6;\r\n            color: var(--text-color);\r\n            line-height: 1.6;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            display: flex;\r\n            justify-content: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 480px;\r\n            width: 100%;\r\n            background: #fff;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);\r\n            overflow: hidden;\r\n        }\r\n        .header {\r\n            background-color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n        }\r\n        .header h1 {\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\r\n            font-weight: 600;\r\n        }\r\n        .header .sub-title {\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n            opacity: 0.9;\r\n            margin-top: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n        .content {\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .answer-banner {\r\n            background-color: var(--correct-color);\r\n            color: white;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-box {\r\n            background-color: var(--highlight-bg);\r\n            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n            border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0;\r\n        }\r\n        .rule-title {\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\r\n            display: block;\r\n        }\r\n        .analysis-section {\r\n            margin-bottom: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .analysis-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--primary-color);\r\n            border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;\r\n            padding-bottom: 5px;\r\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\r\n        }\r\n        .key-term {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            color: var(--accent-color);\r\n        }\r\n        .latin {\r\n            font-style: italic;\r\n            color: #555;\r\n        }\r\n        .distractor {\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n            color: #666;\r\n            margin-top: 10px;\r\n            padding: 10px;\r\n            background: #f9f9f9;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n        }\r\n        .exam-tip {\r\n            background-color: #fff3cd;\r\n            border: 1px solid #ffeeba;\r\n            color: #856404;\r\n            padding: 15px;\r\n            border-radius: var(--border-radius);\r\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\r\n            margin-top: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .exam-tip-title {\r\n            font-weight: bold;\r\n            display: block;\r\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n    <div class=\"header\">\r\n        <h1>MBE 考点解析</h1>\r\n        <div class=\"sub-title\">Constitutional Law | Contracts Clause</div>\r\n    </div>\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"content\">\r\n        <!-- 正确答案展示 -->\r\n        <div class=\"answer-banner\">\r\n            正确答案：B\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 核心考点法则 -->\r\n        <div class=\"rule-box\">\r\n            <span class=\"rule-title\">⚖️ 核心法则 (Legal Rule)</span>\r\n            美国宪法第一条第10款的<span class=\"key-term\">合同条款 (Contracts Clause)</span> 仅限制州政府制定法律损害<b>现存的 (Existing)</b> 合同义务。它并不保护订立<b>未来 (Future)</b> 合同的权利。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 深度解析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"analysis-section\">\r\n            <div class=\"analysis-title\">逻辑推演</div>\r\n            <p>要判定是否违反合同条款，必须遵循以下步骤：</p>\r\n            <ol>\r\n                <li><b>第一步（门槛问题）：</b> 是否存在一个已经生效的合同关系？</li>\r\n                <li><b>第二步：</b> 州法律是否实质性地损害 (Substantially Impair) 了该合同？</li>\r\n                <li><b>第三步：</b> 如果有损害，该法律是否是为了合法的公共目的，且手段是合理的？</li>\r\n            </ol>\r\n            <p>在本题中，分析在<b>第一步</b>就结束了。虽然该女子是合格的教练，且滑雪场也想雇佣她，但题目明确指出“no resort will offer her a contract”（没有滑雪场向她提供合同）。</p>\r\n            <p>因为双方尚未签署合同，仅仅是处于“想要签约”的阶段，所以不存在<b>现存合同 (Existing Contract)</b>。既然没有合同，合同条款就不适用。</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 选项辨析 -->\r\n        <div class=\"analysis-section\">\r\n            <div class=\"analysis-title\">为什么其他选项是错误的？</div>\r\n            \r\n            <div class=\"distractor\">\r\n                <span style=\"color:var(--wrong-color)\">✖ 选项 C 和 D 错误：</span><br>\r\n                这两个选项都试图进行<b>审查标准 (Scrutiny)</b> 的分析（如“合理关联”或“重要政府目标”）。<br><br>\r\n                这是考生的常见陷阱。只有当合同条款<b>适用</b>（即存在合同）时，我们才讨论政府是否有正当理由去损害它。既然本案中没有合同，就不需要讨论政府利益是否重要或手段是否合理。\r\n            </div>\r\n\r\n            <div class=\"distractor\">\r\n                <span style=\"color:var(--wrong-color)\">✖ 选项 A 错误：</span><br>\r\n                虽然合同条款确实既适用于私人合同也适用于公共合同（Public Contracts），但本题的关键点不在于合同的性质，而在于合同<b>根本不存在</b>。\r\n            </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <!-- 考试技巧 -->\r\n        <div class=\"exam-tip\">\r\n            <span class=\"exam-tip-title\">💡 MBE 考试技巧 (Exam Tip)</span>\r\n            当题目问及“Contracts Clause”时，你的第一个反应必须是寻找<b>时间线 (Timeline)</b>：\r\n            <br><br>\r\n            是 <b>先有合同，后有法律</b>？<br>\r\n            还是 <b>先有法律，后签合同</b>？\r\n            <br><br>\r\n            如果是后者（先有法律），该法律就成为未来合同背景的一部分，<b>不违反</b>合同条款。合同条款不保护“预期的”或“未来的”交易机会。\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n</html>",
